- [Narrator] Calf roping time.

245
00:09:57,965 --> 00:09:59,667
- Big, bold, and brassy.

246
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:01,735
- [Narrator] And
there goes Mike.

247
00:10:01,768 --> 00:10:03,737
- [Joel] Now, is that
really an efficient way

248
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:05,272
to bring food to market?

249
00:10:05,305 --> 00:10:06,740
- [Tom Servo] I don't think so.

250
00:10:06,773 --> 00:10:07,675
- [Narrator] Too bad.

251
00:10:07,708 --> 00:10:08,475
Better luck next time, kid.

252
00:10:08,508 --> 00:10:09,977
- Loser.

253
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:12,647
- [Narrator] Sam Wood, champion
calf roper of junior high.

254
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:15,448
- You know, the ironic
thing is Sam's a vegetarian,

255
00:10:15,482 --> 00:10:19,687
but there's nothing exciting
about roping okra patty.

256
00:10:20,722 --> 00:10:21,722
- [Narrator] Put
him down, fella.

257
00:10:21,755 --> 00:10:23,523
- You were adopted.

258
00:10:25,558 --> 00:10:28,828
- Now it's the calf
truss up competition.

259
00:10:30,197 --> 00:10:31,798
- [Narrator] 26 seconds.

260
00:10:31,832 --> 00:10:35,368
- [Tom Servo] Yeah, I'm
hot, that's me pretty much.

261
00:10:35,402 --> 00:10:37,672
- [Joel] We'll never
escape this town.

262
00:10:37,705 --> 00:10:40,640
- [Narrator] Jim Rand, champion
calf roper of senior high.

263
00:10:40,675 --> 00:10:42,343
- And next year's janitor.

264
00:10:42,377 --> 00:10:43,877
- [Narrator] Off his
horse in a flash,

265
00:10:43,910 --> 00:10:46,747
just like his dad
in a big-time rodeo.

266
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:49,150
- [Tom Servo] Holding up the
legacy of secrets and shame.

267
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:51,352
- You know, some
scars don't heal.

268
00:10:51,385 --> 00:10:53,287
Up next is another young feller.

269
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,988
- [Narrator] 16 seconds.

270
00:10:55,022 --> 00:10:56,623
- [Joel] And the
crowd goes wild.

271
00:10:56,657 --> 00:10:58,625
- [All] Yay.

272
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,193
- [Narrator] Calf
riders, stand by.

273
00:11:00,227 --> 00:11:02,630
- [Joel] I don't really
know what I'm doing!

274
00:11:02,663 --> 00:11:03,830
Oh!

275
00:11:03,863 --> 00:11:05,867
- Why can't Johnny ride?

276
00:11:12,072 --> 00:11:14,142
- [Narrator] Here comes Bobby,

277
00:11:14,175 --> 00:11:15,675
and there he goes.

278
00:11:15,710 --> 00:11:19,180
- [Joel] Fortunately, Bobby
didn't need his spine.

279
00:11:19,213 --> 00:11:21,148
- [Narrator] The girls
aren't bashful, either.

280
00:11:21,182 --> 00:11:23,683
- Like my friend Geeky,
that which does not kill you

281
00:11:23,717 --> 00:11:25,452
makes you stronger.

282
00:11:27,388 --> 00:11:28,622
- [Tom Servo] Oh,
here comes this guy.

283
00:11:28,655 --> 00:11:29,423
- [Narrator] And there
goes the youngest

284
00:11:29,457 --> 00:11:30,792
bull rider of them all.

285
00:11:30,825 --> 00:11:33,927
- [Tom Servo] Ow, dat der
drat it, aw gee criminy.

286
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:37,297
- [Joel] Go ahead, strip me
of my dignity at age four.

287
00:11:37,330 --> 00:11:39,333
What are you looking at!

288
00:11:40,902 --> 00:11:43,303
- [Narrator] Kind of
tall for a calf rider.

289
00:11:43,337 --> 00:11:45,005
- Not any more.

290
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:46,207
- [Narrator] Bettie's
in high school.

291
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,508
- [Joel] Used to be.

292
00:11:47,542 --> 00:11:48,508
- [Narrator] You
should see the boys

293
00:11:48,542 --> 00:11:50,477
when she goes square dancing.

294
00:11:50,510 --> 00:11:53,980
- [Tom Servo] Yeah, they
buck her off right away.

295
00:12:02,188 --> 00:12:04,592
- Oh, she can't take a dare.

296
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:10,463
- [Joel] Anybody get
a license number?

297
00:12:13,767 --> 00:12:15,668
- [Narrator] It's all
the same for Mary Lou,

298
00:12:15,702 --> 00:12:18,105
beauty contest or calf riding.

299
00:12:18,138 --> 00:12:19,407
- [Tom Servo] Uh,
oatmeal's done.

300
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,275
- [Narrator] She
can win 'em both.

301
00:12:21,308 --> 00:12:22,408
Yes sir.

302
00:12:22,443 --> 00:12:23,310
- Yes, yes.

303
00:12:24,812 --> 00:12:28,615
- [Joel] Hey honey, want to
come to my pen for drinks later?

304
00:12:28,682 --> 00:12:29,783
And the crowd goes wild.

305
00:12:29,783 --> 00:12:30,785
- [All] Yay.

306
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:35,755
- [Narrator] Senior
high bull riding.

307
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:36,823
- [Tom Servo] Fresh
off the grill.

308
00:12:36,857 --> 00:12:38,558
- [Narrator] This Angus
bull is no hobby horse.

309
00:12:38,592 --> 00:12:40,327
- No, it's garbage.

310
00:12:41,795 --> 00:12:44,165
- [Tom Servo] He's
a moveable feast.

311
00:12:47,502 --> 00:12:49,903
- [Narrator] Will you look
at that bull, he's really--

312
00:12:49,937 --> 00:12:53,273
- [Tom Servo] Oh, take
the rope off my groin.

313
00:12:59,613 --> 00:13:01,948
- [Joel] Here comes the
last surviving castrati.

314
00:13:01,948 --> 00:13:04,752
- [Narrator] Only two years
ago he was still riding calves.

315
00:13:04,785 --> 00:13:07,420
- Now he sells pencil and
string on street corners.

316
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:09,890
- [Narrator] Dad's going to
be mighty proud of him today.

317
00:13:09,923 --> 00:13:11,625
- If he can find him.

318
00:13:17,965 --> 00:13:20,067
Oh no, oh no, this is wrong.

319
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:22,570
I signed up for debate!

320
00:13:22,603 --> 00:13:23,570
- [Narrator] Just six seconds.

321
00:13:23,603 --> 00:13:25,105
- [Tom Servo] Over Tokyo.

322
00:13:25,138 --> 00:13:26,873
- [Narrator] And here's
Slash Barcay's meanest bronc.

323
00:13:26,907 --> 00:13:29,310
- That horse has
got Air Jordan's on.

324
00:13:29,343 --> 00:13:31,478
- [Narrator] Sits him like
he was glued to the saddle.

325
00:13:31,512 --> 00:13:32,278
- I am!

326
00:13:35,348 --> 00:13:39,387
- [Tom Servo] Hey, hey,
you're crowding my lane.

327
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:40,687
- [Joel] And the
crowd goes wild.

328
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:42,255
- [All] Yay.

329
00:13:42,288 --> 00:13:43,590
- [Narrator] Okay
Glen, get out there

330
00:13:43,623 --> 00:13:44,692
and show them how to do it.

331
00:13:44,725 --> 00:13:47,562
- [Joel] Or don't
come home tonight.

332
00:13:50,130 --> 00:13:51,865
- I am not an animal.

333
00:13:53,633 --> 00:13:56,070
- [Narrator] Watch out,
that ground's awful hard.

334
00:13:56,103 --> 00:13:57,872
- [Joel] Life is awful hard.

335
00:13:57,905 --> 00:14:00,340
- [Narrator] We sure
had us a junior rodeo.

336
00:14:00,373 --> 00:14:02,175
- Next week, geriatric rodeo.

337
00:14:02,208 --> 00:14:04,378
- [Narrator] And then it
came prize giving time.

338
00:14:04,412 --> 00:14:07,615
- [Tom Servo] First
price, bronze cow chips.

339
00:14:08,782 --> 00:14:10,450
- [Narrator] Prizes for winning.

340
00:14:10,483 --> 00:14:11,652
- Even George F.
Kaufman won a prize.

341
00:14:11,685 --> 00:14:13,487
- [Narrator] And
prizes for trying.

342
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:17,457
- [Joel] In other
words, bitter failure.

343
00:14:17,490 --> 00:14:18,858
- It's Hayley Mills.

344
00:14:18,892 --> 00:14:20,560
- Sure loved you
in The Parent Trap.

345
00:14:20,593 --> 00:14:24,298
- [Narrator] Yes sirree, the
junior rodeo is here to stay,

346
00:14:24,332 --> 00:14:28,535
and nobody's happier about it
than old-timer Billy Slater.

347
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:31,305
- [Tom Servo] It's sad, really.

348
00:14:31,338 --> 00:14:35,542
♪ And the guys are
not clowning all day

349
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:41,248
(upbeat music)

350
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:48,388
- [Narrator] Those
who hunt by night

351
00:14:48,422 --> 00:14:51,325
will tell you that the
wildest and most vicious

352
00:14:51,358 --> 00:14:52,693
of all animals--

353
00:14:52,727 --> 00:14:53,627
- [Tom Servo] Are in Vegas?

354
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:54,962
- [Narrator] Is the tiny shrew.

355
00:14:54,995 --> 00:14:56,297
- [All] A shrew?

356
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:59,633
- [Narrator] Feeds only
by the dark of the moon.

357
00:14:59,667 --> 00:15:01,202
- Yeah, just go with
us on this, okay?

358
00:15:01,235 --> 00:15:02,937
- [Narrator] He must
eat his own body weight

359
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:04,638
every few hours.

360
00:15:04,672 --> 00:15:05,940
- [Tom Servo] Plus
a delicious shake.

361
00:15:05,973 --> 00:15:09,810
- [Narrator] And the
shrew devours everything,

362
00:15:09,843 --> 00:15:12,512
bones, flesh,
marrow, everything.

363
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:15,448
- He can really
tuck away a moth.

364
00:15:15,482 --> 00:15:19,453
- [Narrator] First in
Alaska, and then invading

365
00:15:19,487 --> 00:15:23,457
steadily southward, there
were reports of a new species.

366
00:15:24,658 --> 00:15:25,858
- [Joel] A fun species.

367
00:15:25,892 --> 00:15:28,328
- [Narrator] The
giant killer shrew.

368
00:15:28,362 --> 00:15:29,297
- So there!

369
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:32,032
- The.
- The.

370
00:15:32,065 --> 00:15:33,433
- Killer.
- Killer.

371
00:15:33,467 --> 00:15:34,435
- Shrews.
- Shrews.

372
00:15:34,468 --> 00:15:38,372
- Starring Joan Collins
and Jackie Collins.

373
00:15:38,405 --> 00:15:41,308
- [Joel] Oh, Ingrid is
good, but James is best.

374
00:15:41,342 --> 00:15:42,810
- [Tom Servo] I think so.

375
00:15:49,282 --> 00:15:51,618
- [Joel] Based on a
novel by William Shatner.

376
00:15:51,652 --> 00:15:52,920
Spock.

377
00:15:52,953 --> 00:15:55,155
- Oh, the great
William M. Cline.

378
00:15:55,188 --> 00:15:56,623
Wilfred (chuckles).

379
00:15:56,657 --> 00:15:58,658
- [Tom Servo] Oh, I passed
a blue stone last night,

380
00:15:58,692 --> 00:16:00,493
let me tell you.

381
00:16:00,527 --> 00:16:01,795
- [Joel] No shrews were hurt

382
00:16:01,828 --> 00:16:03,463
during the making
of this picture.

383
00:16:03,497 --> 00:16:05,598
- [Tom Servo] Well, a few, but.

384
00:16:07,835 --> 00:16:09,268
Big Ben Chapman.

385
00:16:11,472 --> 00:16:14,173
- Matthew, if you ain't
the orneriest sprout

386
00:16:14,207 --> 00:16:16,110
that ever jumped on my lawn.

387
00:16:16,143 --> 00:16:17,477
- [Joel] Hey, Ray Kellogg,

388
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:19,980
he directed The
Giant Gila Monster.

389
00:16:20,013 --> 00:16:21,315
- [Tom Servo] No, no!

390
00:16:24,418 --> 00:16:25,385
Oh, it's Robert Maxwell's boat.

391
00:16:25,418 --> 00:16:27,487
Mr. Maxwell, Mr. Maxwell.

392
00:16:29,255 --> 00:16:32,125
- [Joel] Hey, it's PT
90210, check it out.

393
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:34,462
- Sure is a lot of
quiet out there.

394
00:16:34,495 --> 00:16:35,595
- Too lot of quiet.

395
00:16:35,628 --> 00:16:37,497
- Almost smell it, can't you?

396
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:38,298
- [Joel] No, that's me.

397
00:16:38,332 --> 00:16:40,133
- No, but I can feel it.

398
00:16:40,167 --> 00:16:41,135
The pressure's dropped so fast,

399
00:16:41,168 --> 00:16:43,437
it's almost made my ears pop.

400
00:16:43,470 --> 00:16:44,972
- [Joel] Chew gum.

401
00:16:45,005 --> 00:16:48,575
- Hurricane's got definite
ways of telling you it's there.

402
00:16:48,608 --> 00:16:49,943
Where is it?

403
00:16:49,977 --> 00:16:51,112
- I thought you knew.

404
00:16:51,145 --> 00:16:52,345
- Dead ahead.

405
00:16:52,378 --> 00:16:53,547
- [Joel] Do you think I'm heavy?

406
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:55,382
- What's that mean to us.

407
00:16:55,382 --> 00:16:57,083
- Now boy, that puts our port
right in the middle of it.

408
00:16:57,117 --> 00:16:58,485
- Oh God help me.

409
00:17:02,422 --> 00:17:04,057
- There's a cove on
the lee side, though.

410
00:17:04,090 --> 00:17:05,892
We'll snuggle up close to
the bluff and ride it out.

411
00:17:05,925 --> 00:17:08,128
- We most certainly will not.

412
00:17:08,162 --> 00:17:12,398
- Well, the chart shows it's
good holding ground, it's clay.

413
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:14,468
- [Joel] Yep.

414
00:17:14,502 --> 00:17:15,468
- You know something?

415
00:17:15,502 --> 00:17:16,570
- [Joel] What?

416
00:17:16,603 --> 00:17:17,872
- If this thing had
an automatic pilot,

417
00:17:17,905 --> 00:17:19,105
I wouldn't have to
put up with you.

418
00:17:19,138 --> 00:17:20,940
- Then you wouldn't
have nobody to chew out.

419
00:17:20,973 --> 00:17:23,443
- [Tom Servo] Yeah, wait til
the whip comes down, white boy.

420
00:17:23,477 --> 00:17:25,078
- Be there in a couple of hours,

421
00:17:25,112 --> 00:17:27,247
these mills of
yours keep running.

422
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:30,450
- Look, automatic pilots
can't play dixieland jazz

423
00:17:30,483 --> 00:17:32,552
on their banjos like I can.

424
00:17:32,585 --> 00:17:33,587
- (laughs) Good point.

425
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:36,390
- What the heck did that mean?

426
00:17:36,423 --> 00:17:38,125
- [Joel] They're trolling
kind of fast, aren't they?

427
00:17:38,158 --> 00:17:40,760
- [Tom Servo] They're
gonna lose bait.

428
00:17:42,462 --> 00:17:43,397
- Hey, Rook.

429
00:17:43,430 --> 00:17:44,632
Rook, come here.

430
00:17:44,665 --> 00:17:47,300
- These things make
everything look bigger!

431
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:48,568
- Take a look.

432
00:17:49,470 --> 00:17:51,405
There she is, dead ahead.

433
00:17:51,438 --> 00:17:55,442
- Oh yeah, it's Gilligan's
Island, the headhunter episode.

434
00:17:55,475 --> 00:17:58,512
- Man, that sure do look good.

435
00:17:58,545 --> 00:18:00,080
- [Joel] Mrs. Howell?

436
00:18:00,113 --> 00:18:02,148
- Man named Craigis owns
the island, does he?

437
00:18:02,182 --> 00:18:03,817
- That's the name on the
crate, Dr. Milo Craigis.

438
00:18:03,850 --> 00:18:06,153
- We'll unload tomorrow.

439
00:18:06,187 --> 00:18:07,753
I don't want this craft
sitting high in the water

440
00:18:07,788 --> 00:18:09,088
when that blow hits.

441
00:18:09,122 --> 00:18:10,157
- [Tom Servo] Yes, yes.

442
00:18:10,190 --> 00:18:11,325
- With a lot of water under?

443
00:18:11,358 --> 00:18:12,358
- That's right.

444
00:18:12,392 --> 00:18:14,160
That sea won't pick
up in that cove,

445
00:18:14,193 --> 00:18:17,530
that wind'll have it
whipping around like a kite.

446
00:18:17,563 --> 00:18:19,767
Step forward and break out
the heavy weather hook.

447
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,368
Check and make sure
it's free to run.

448
00:18:21,402 --> 00:18:24,103
- Yeah, but a heavy weather
hook can't play dixieland jazz.

449
00:18:24,137 --> 00:18:26,240
- Alright, Joel, alright.

450
00:18:27,407 --> 00:18:29,108
- Hey, say, like
Robinson Crusoe,

451
00:18:29,142 --> 00:18:31,445
this is as primitive as can be.

452
00:18:31,478 --> 00:18:34,047
- Bet Robinson Crusoe
can't play dixieland jazz.

453
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:36,483
- Would you knock it off
about dixieland jazz?

454
00:18:36,550 --> 00:18:39,218
- Oh, I know this, this is
the famous dock walking scene.

455
00:18:39,252 --> 00:18:40,587
You know, this whole take
was done in one shot.

456
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:43,523
It's a planned sequence, like
the opening of Touch of Evil

457
00:18:43,557 --> 00:18:45,325
and the Copa Cabana
scene in Goodfellows.

458
00:18:45,358 --> 00:18:47,493
This is virtuoso
filmmaking, fellas,

459
00:18:47,527 --> 00:18:48,528
you got to see it to believe it.

460
00:18:48,562 --> 00:18:50,030
Now Brian De Palma
used this in um,

461
00:18:50,063 --> 00:18:52,532
in, in Bonfire of the Vanities,

462
00:18:52,565 --> 00:18:55,568
really exciting,
it's splendiferous.

463
00:19:01,073 --> 00:19:03,343
- Well, we've covered
the waterfront.

464
00:19:03,377 --> 00:19:05,212
- Ah, she'll ride like a duck.

465
00:19:05,245 --> 00:19:06,313
If she swings too
far to starboard,

466
00:19:06,347 --> 00:19:07,982
we might have to take
a check line to shore.

467
00:19:08,015 --> 00:19:09,448
- [Tom Servo] Yeah, whatever.

468
00:19:09,517 --> 00:19:12,685
- Hey, Rook, take a
slant up that trail.

469
00:19:12,718 --> 00:19:15,122
- Hey, this island's
got oak trees!

470
00:19:15,155 --> 00:19:17,157
- Now that's a rather strange
set up, wouldn't you say?

471
00:19:17,190 --> 00:19:18,825
- Yeah, but the
punchline makes it work.

472
00:19:18,858 --> 00:19:20,560
- Looks like somebody's
getting rid of somebody.

473
00:19:20,593 --> 00:19:21,362
- [Joel] Sometime.

474
00:19:21,395 --> 00:19:23,130
- Maybe.

475
00:19:23,163 --> 00:19:24,230
Hard to tell.

476
00:19:25,498 --> 00:19:27,500
- But I bet they can't
play dixieland jazz--

477
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:28,702
- [Tom Servo] Shut up.

478
00:19:30,237 --> 00:19:33,940
- Like Columbus, we claim
this island for, oh, hi.

479
00:19:38,445 --> 00:19:42,315
- [Joel] Uh, I'm the
temp you ordered.

480
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:43,517
- I'm Dr. Craigis.

481
00:19:43,550 --> 00:19:44,885
- Yeah, right, whatever,
who's the lady?

482
00:19:44,918 --> 00:19:46,453
- Got your supplies aboard.

483
00:19:46,487 --> 00:19:47,687
- That's good.

484
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:49,757
Nothing wrong with
Captain Peterson, I hope.

485
00:19:49,790 --> 00:19:50,757
- Well, I wouldn't know.

486
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:52,325
- Ever heard of Slim Fast?

487
00:19:52,358 --> 00:19:53,860
- I just bought his run.

488
00:19:53,893 --> 00:19:55,462
- Oh, I see.

489
00:19:55,495 --> 00:19:57,197
Were you able to fill my order?

490
00:19:57,230 --> 00:19:58,465
- Everything on the list.

491
00:19:58,498 --> 00:19:59,265
Here's the manifest.

492
00:19:59,298 --> 00:20:00,867
- [Tom Servo] Destiny.

493
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:04,503
- Missing last week's supply
has run us a little short.

494
00:20:04,537 --> 00:20:08,008
Captain, after you've unloaded,
I have a passenger for you.

495
00:20:08,042 --> 00:20:08,842
Ann.

496
00:20:10,077 --> 00:20:12,478
Captain Sherman, this is
my daughter Ann Craigis.

497
00:20:12,512 --> 00:20:13,580
- So hands off.

498
00:20:14,413 --> 00:20:16,617
- Well, so you're the passenger.

499
00:20:16,683 --> 00:20:18,918
- That's right, captain.

500
00:20:18,952 --> 00:20:21,288
- Well, it's going to be
nice having you aboard.

501
00:20:21,322 --> 00:20:22,923
I'm getting a little tired
of looking at Griswald.

502
00:20:22,957 --> 00:20:24,190
- [Joel] Can you
play dixieland jazz?

503
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:26,927
- We're not leaving today.

504
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,128
- [Joel] Oh, well, I--

505
00:20:28,162 --> 00:20:28,928
- [Tom Servo] Huh?

506
00:20:28,962 --> 00:20:29,697
Huh?

507
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:31,298
Oh?

508
00:20:31,332 --> 00:20:33,500
- In fact, we're
not even unloading.

509
00:20:33,533 --> 00:20:34,968
- In fact, we don't even exist.

510
00:20:35,002 --> 00:20:38,138
- That load will cut
the roll in half.

511
00:20:38,172 --> 00:20:41,375
- Now wait, you don't
have a line yet.

512
00:20:41,408 --> 00:20:42,708
- Yes, animals.

513
00:20:43,877 --> 00:20:46,145
- Game or otherwise.

514
00:20:46,178 --> 00:20:50,250
- Under certain conditions,
it could be dangerous.

515
00:20:50,283 --> 00:20:52,618
- [Joel] He's right, you know.

516
00:20:52,652 --> 00:20:54,988
- Hey Rook, you want
to shake the kinks out,

517
00:20:55,022 --> 00:20:56,290
limber up a little.

518
00:20:56,323 --> 00:20:57,423
- Not me, captain,
but you go right ahead

519
00:20:57,457 --> 00:20:59,125
and stretch your legs.

520
00:20:59,158 --> 00:21:00,227
That ship's going
to be bucking like

521
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:01,928
a bucking bronco before long.

522
00:21:01,962 --> 00:21:03,663
'Sides, I got some
work left to do.

523
00:21:03,697 --> 00:21:05,432
- A simple yes or no will do.

524
00:21:05,465 --> 00:21:07,433
- If you come
ashore, wear a gun.

525
00:21:07,467 --> 00:21:08,435
- Got you, captain.

526
00:21:08,468 --> 00:21:09,402
- [Tom Servo] And if
you go to San Francisco,

527
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,305
wear some flowers in your hair.

528
00:21:11,338 --> 00:21:12,838
- [Joel] Gotcha, captain.

529
00:21:12,872 --> 00:21:16,410
Oh, he must be scouting
locations for Dukes of Hazzard.

530
00:21:16,443 --> 00:21:17,210
- Ooh.

531
00:21:18,678 --> 00:21:21,213
Boss Hogg'll love this place.

532
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:26,887
- [Tom Servo] I'd say
they went a bit overboard

533
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,155
on the fence.

534
00:21:28,188 --> 00:21:29,555
- [Joel] No sense
of perspective.

535
00:21:29,588 --> 00:21:30,290
- [Tom Servo] You know, they
should have put a gate in it,

536
00:21:30,323 --> 00:21:31,792
for crying out loud.

537
00:21:34,795 --> 00:21:37,930
- [Joel] I've fallen in with a
group of ham radio operators.

538
00:21:37,963 --> 00:21:40,300
- When I told you
about the hurricane,

539
00:21:40,333 --> 00:21:42,102
you acted like you didn't
know anything about it.

540
00:21:42,135 --> 00:21:43,403
- Hurricane Carter?

541
00:21:43,437 --> 00:21:45,238
- What's the matter,
your set broken down?

542
00:21:45,272 --> 00:21:46,305
- We've been out
of communication

543
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:47,607
for more than a week, captain.

544
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,275
- Can it be fixed?

545
00:21:50,177 --> 00:21:52,412
- Totally out of commission.

546
00:21:52,445 --> 00:21:53,313
- What he said.

547
00:21:53,347 --> 00:21:54,982
- My assistant.

548
00:21:55,015 --> 00:21:56,617
Mr. Farrell, Jerry Farrell.

549
00:21:56,650 --> 00:21:58,118
- Jerry Farrell?

550
00:21:58,152 --> 00:22:00,087
Hey, did he go to Haroldson
Elementary School?

551
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:02,288
- [Joel] Hey, Freddy Fender.

552
00:22:04,423 --> 00:22:08,062
- Father, perhaps the
captain will enjoy a drink.

553
00:22:08,095 --> 00:22:10,263
- Well, of course.

554
00:22:10,297 --> 00:22:11,798
Will you join us in a cocktail?

555
00:22:11,832 --> 00:22:14,267
- Well, I've never been known
to turn down a drink yet.

556
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:15,635
I'll be glad to accept.

557
00:22:15,668 --> 00:22:17,370
- I've been known to beg for
them, as a matter of fact.

558
00:22:17,403 --> 00:22:19,238
- In that case
we'll have martinis.

559
00:22:19,272 --> 00:22:20,407
Mario.

560
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:21,442
- Si, senor.

561
00:22:21,475 --> 00:22:23,410
- Mix them, please.

562
00:22:23,443 --> 00:22:26,278
- Mix 'em please,
what's he talking about?

563
00:22:26,312 --> 00:22:27,880
- [Joel] What a scene.

564
00:22:27,913 --> 00:22:29,348
- Right this way, captain.

565
00:22:29,415 --> 00:22:30,450
- You know those
little cocktail napkins

566
00:22:30,517 --> 00:22:31,685
with the jokes on them?

567
00:22:31,718 --> 00:22:34,053
I love those little guys.

568
00:22:34,087 --> 00:22:37,390
- [Tom Servo] Uh, check your
gun at the door, Festus.

569
00:22:37,423 --> 00:22:39,225
- [Joel] There, bad door.

570
00:22:40,727 --> 00:22:42,562
Okay, don't say hi, ga.

571
00:22:45,132 --> 00:22:47,167
- Sounds like Flash Gordon.

572
00:22:48,668 --> 00:22:49,870
- [Tom Servo] What a dump.

573
00:22:49,903 --> 00:22:51,037
Who said that, George?

574
00:22:51,070 --> 00:22:52,905
- You have everything
here you need?

575
00:22:52,938 --> 00:22:55,042
- We are self-sufficient here.

576
00:22:55,075 --> 00:22:58,912
We have cows for fresh milk,
chickens for fresh eggs.

577
00:22:58,945 --> 00:23:01,147
- [Tom Servo] Gin, rum,
pickled eggs, mixers.

578
00:23:01,180 --> 00:23:03,048
- Sort of a world all your own.

579
00:23:03,083 --> 00:23:04,985
- That's exactly what
I've tried to create.

580
00:23:05,018 --> 00:23:07,387
- Well, to each his own.

581
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:08,988
If you have to be
isolated for your work,

582
00:23:09,022 --> 00:23:10,790
you've picked a
lonely little island.

583
00:23:10,823 --> 00:23:12,358
- What are you getting
at, what's your point?

584
00:23:12,392 --> 00:23:14,828
- Excuse me, please,
I think I'll change.

585
00:23:14,862 --> 00:23:16,128
- Why'd you go and
say that to her?

586
00:23:16,162 --> 00:23:17,530
Geez, let's leave.

587
00:23:19,532 --> 00:23:22,368
(doors closing)

588
00:23:29,242 --> 00:23:30,843
- Tom, I knew that
shirt was going to

589
00:23:30,877 --> 00:23:32,912
push some bad buttons for
Joel and get him started

590
00:23:32,945 --> 00:23:35,482
doing that Will Rogers thing
he's been talking about.

591
00:23:35,515 --> 00:23:36,783
- And you were right, Crow.

592
00:23:36,850 --> 00:23:38,552
By the way, I do love
those pants (laughs).

593
00:23:38,585 --> 00:23:40,820
- Oh, I ought to pants you.
- Shh, here he comes.

594
00:23:40,853 --> 00:23:43,022
- Well, howdy folks,
how you doing?

595
00:23:43,055 --> 00:23:44,757
You know, I've been
listening to what

596
00:23:44,792 --> 00:23:46,760
the President's
been doing, and it

597
00:23:46,793 --> 00:23:48,128
kind of seems to
me like he's trying

598
00:23:48,162 --> 00:23:51,498
to crawl into the wrong end
of the cracker barrel, hyuck.

599
00:23:51,532 --> 00:23:53,200
- Moo.

600
00:23:53,233 --> 00:23:54,300
- Uh, bristle, I guess.

601
00:23:54,333 --> 00:23:55,602
- Yeah, I'm a lot
like you folks.

602
00:23:55,635 --> 00:23:57,470
I'm simple, you know,
and I been hearing

603
00:23:57,503 --> 00:24:00,340
the President go on and on,
and it kind of seems to me

604
00:24:00,373 --> 00:24:02,475
like the polecat's
got caught in the cow

605
00:24:02,508 --> 00:24:05,278
and it's time for the hound dog
to skitter him out of there.

606
00:24:05,312 --> 00:24:06,480
(Tom Servo moos)

607
00:24:06,513 --> 00:24:07,513
- Hey, this is fun.

608
00:24:07,547 --> 00:24:08,448
(moos)

609
00:24:08,482 --> 00:24:09,148
- Pretty good at it, too.

610
00:24:09,215 --> 00:24:10,450
Bristle, bristle.

611
00:24:10,517 --> 00:24:11,752
- Oh yeah, you know,
kind of reminds me

612
00:24:11,785 --> 00:24:14,287
of Aunt Martha's
mustache, you know.

613
00:24:14,320 --> 00:24:17,123
Makes a fella hungry for some
down home dogfish, don't it.

614
00:24:17,157 --> 00:24:18,458
- What?

615
00:24:18,492 --> 00:24:21,260
- The rumors of my death have
been greatly exaggerated.

616
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:22,762
- That's not Will Rogers.

617
00:24:22,795 --> 00:24:24,030
(moos)

618
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:25,865
- Yup, it's not
over til it's over.

619
00:24:25,898 --> 00:24:27,200
- And that's Casey Stengel.

620
00:24:27,233 --> 00:24:28,268
What's he doing?

621
00:24:28,302 --> 00:24:29,135
- I don't know,
it's crazy there.

622
00:24:29,168 --> 00:24:30,137
- Yup, yup, yup.

623
00:24:30,170 --> 00:24:32,172
Oh, well everything
I love is either

624
00:24:32,205 --> 00:24:34,207
illegal, immoral, or fattening.

625
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:35,542
Take a bite out of crime.

626
00:24:35,575 --> 00:24:37,443
- Wait a minute, Alexander
Walcott and McGruff?

627
00:24:37,477 --> 00:24:38,178
He's all over the map.

628
00:24:38,212 --> 00:24:39,112
Joel, you okay?

629
00:24:39,145 --> 00:24:40,113
Come here, buddy (whistles).

630
00:24:40,147 --> 00:24:41,815
- Yup, we will bury you.

631
00:24:41,848 --> 00:24:42,815
- Khrushchev?

632
00:24:42,882 --> 00:24:44,083
Oh, Joel.

633
00:24:44,117 --> 00:24:47,420
- Yup, baseball been
berry, berry good to me.

634
00:24:47,453 --> 00:24:48,988
- Oh, now he's doing
Garrett Morris.

635
00:24:49,022 --> 00:24:49,990
- Really sad.

636
00:24:50,023 --> 00:24:50,790
- Just toying with us.

637
00:24:50,823 --> 00:24:52,125
Let's get out of here.

638
00:24:52,158 --> 00:24:54,827
- Anybody here seen
my old friend John?

639
00:24:54,862 --> 00:24:56,630
- Ah, ah, Joel, let me go!

640
00:24:56,663 --> 00:24:58,398
I want to go iron my pants!

641
00:24:58,432 --> 00:25:00,900
- Yup, yup, yup, it's
morning in America.

642
00:25:00,933 --> 00:25:02,468
- No, it is not.

643
00:25:02,502 --> 00:25:03,803
- Yup.

644
00:25:03,837 --> 00:25:06,673
One fish, two fish,
red fish, blue fish.

645
00:25:06,707 --> 00:25:09,108
(light music)

646
00:25:12,945 --> 00:25:15,248
- Hey, I thought, you're
gonna hurt somebody with this.

647
00:25:15,282 --> 00:25:16,917
- [Tom Servo] Well,
it was your idea.

648
00:25:16,983 --> 00:25:18,952
- I can understand that.

649
00:25:20,653 --> 00:25:21,420
- [Joel] Ouch!

650
00:25:21,453 --> 00:25:22,322
- Sorry.

651
00:25:22,355 --> 00:25:24,323
- [Joel] How would you know?

652
00:25:24,357 --> 00:25:25,158
- Hey.

653
00:25:26,092 --> 00:25:27,193
Bob Clampett.

654
00:25:32,298 --> 00:25:34,935
- [Tom Servo] So how's your
novel coming along there?

655
00:25:34,968 --> 00:25:35,935
- Radford.

656
00:25:35,968 --> 00:25:37,737
- [Joel] Rapid?

657
00:25:37,770 --> 00:25:39,038
Bathroom?

658
00:25:39,072 --> 00:25:40,240
- Radford, would you
please step over here.

659
00:25:40,273 --> 00:25:42,075
- [Joel] Rapid, bathroom?

660
00:25:42,108 --> 00:25:44,110
- Just a second, doc.

661
00:25:44,143 --> 00:25:47,080
- [Joel] Yes, this is
our resident novelist,
Rapid Bathroom.

662
00:25:47,113 --> 00:25:48,515
- Doctor Baines.

663
00:25:49,983 --> 00:25:52,018
- There's no need to shout,
doctor, I'm right here.

664
00:25:52,052 --> 00:25:54,220
- I'd like you to meet
Captain Thorne Sherman.

665
00:25:54,253 --> 00:25:56,890
- [Joel] Stone Shrimp?

666
00:25:56,923 --> 00:25:58,725
- How do you do?

667
00:25:58,758 --> 00:26:00,593
- Two new litters
since lunch, doctor.

668
00:26:00,627 --> 00:26:02,228
Both support GT-116.

669
00:26:03,095 --> 00:26:04,697
- That's good, but uh--

670
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:07,700
- We can breed them to the 205
group in about three weeks.

671
00:26:07,733 --> 00:26:09,268
But I'd prefer to
wait and expose

672
00:26:09,302 --> 00:26:10,603
about half of them to the--

673
00:26:10,637 --> 00:26:12,738
- [Joel] Hey, relax.

674
00:26:12,772 --> 00:26:14,073
- If you agree.

675
00:26:15,475 --> 00:26:16,475
- Good idea.

676
00:26:17,977 --> 00:26:19,545
Do you know there's
a hurricane coming?

677
00:26:19,578 --> 00:26:22,115
- No, but if you hum a few bars.

678
00:26:22,148 --> 00:26:24,283
- Well I don't
suppose there's much

679
00:26:24,317 --> 00:26:26,252
we can do about that.

680
00:26:27,587 --> 00:26:29,222
Glad to meet you.

681
00:26:29,255 --> 00:26:32,825
- [Joel] Could you get me a
few Denver Pyle autographs?

682
00:26:34,260 --> 00:26:36,195
- [Tom Servo] We need
the eggs, as they say.

683
00:26:36,228 --> 00:26:37,163
- You have to excuse Radford.

684
00:26:37,197 --> 00:26:38,398
- [Joel] He smells.

685
00:26:38,432 --> 00:26:40,033
- Anything that does
not concern his project

686
00:26:40,067 --> 00:26:41,433
does not get through to him.

687
00:26:41,467 --> 00:26:43,437
Brilliant mind.

688
00:26:43,470 --> 00:26:44,770
He would starve to death

689
00:26:44,803 --> 00:26:46,105
if someone didn't
remind him to eat.

690
00:26:46,138 --> 00:26:47,073
- Must be very interesting work.

691
00:26:47,107 --> 00:26:48,107
What's his field?

692
00:26:48,140 --> 00:26:48,908
- [Tom Servo] Of dreams.

693
00:26:48,942 --> 00:26:50,210
- Biology.

694
00:26:50,243 --> 00:26:52,045
He specializes in
genetics, heredity.

695
00:26:52,078 --> 00:26:54,780
- I'm afraid my interest doesn't
run in that line, you know.

696
00:26:54,813 --> 00:26:55,615
- Get out.

697
00:26:56,717 --> 00:26:58,150
- If you could
isolate and identify

698
00:26:58,183 --> 00:27:00,020
the inherited
factor in each gene.

699
00:27:00,053 --> 00:27:01,053
- Now wait a minute, I'm afraid

700
00:27:01,087 --> 00:27:03,022
I'm not very good
with pure research.

701
00:27:03,055 --> 00:27:05,258
- This is practical research.

702
00:27:05,292 --> 00:27:06,827
- I'm not good at that, either.

703
00:27:06,860 --> 00:27:08,227
- The theory among mammals,
the smaller the size,

704
00:27:08,260 --> 00:27:11,998
the higher the metabolism
and shorter the lifespan.

705
00:27:12,032 --> 00:27:13,032
- Is that right.

706
00:27:13,065 --> 00:27:15,168
- Well, I'm attempting
to decrease the size

707
00:27:15,202 --> 00:27:17,603
by maintaining a low metabolism

708
00:27:17,637 --> 00:27:19,938
and resultant a longer lifespan.

709
00:27:19,972 --> 00:27:21,040
- What reason?

710
00:27:21,073 --> 00:27:22,675
- You think he'd come up
with a hair growth thing

711
00:27:22,708 --> 00:27:23,943
if he was so smart.

712
00:27:23,977 --> 00:27:26,780
- I'd like to hit
you really hard.

713
00:27:27,580 --> 00:27:29,215
- In time.

714
00:27:29,215 --> 00:27:31,017
- [Joel] Hey, it's Cousin
Marilyn from the Munsters.

715
00:27:31,050 --> 00:27:32,052
- Oh.

716
00:27:33,052 --> 00:27:34,987
- If we were half as
big as we were now,

717
00:27:35,022 --> 00:27:38,358
we could live twice as long
on our natural resources.

718
00:27:38,392 --> 00:27:39,625
- She's got her
apron on backwards.

719
00:27:39,658 --> 00:27:41,627
- Father, may I speak
with you a moment?

720
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:44,297
Will you please
excuse us, captain?

721
00:27:44,330 --> 00:27:46,632
- Well, providing
you drop the captain.

722
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:47,400
- [Tom Servo] Ouch.

723
00:27:47,433 --> 00:27:49,135
- I prefer Thorne.

724
00:27:49,168 --> 00:27:53,072
- Dad, this scientist thing is
cute, but it's wearing thin.

725
00:27:53,105 --> 00:27:56,008
- [Joel] Mm hmm,
that's good booze.

726
00:27:58,378 --> 00:28:00,413
- Tell him, tell him now.

727
00:28:02,782 --> 00:28:04,017
- Tell me something, doctor.

728
00:28:04,050 --> 00:28:05,118
- [Joel] Why do
fools fall in love?

729
00:28:05,152 --> 00:28:06,953
- Has a hurricane ever
hit this island before

730
00:28:06,987 --> 00:28:08,020
that you know of?

731
00:28:08,053 --> 00:28:09,055
- I wouldn't know.

732
00:28:09,088 --> 00:28:10,857
We've only been
here nine months,

733
00:28:10,890 --> 00:28:12,892
and this place has been
unoccupied for years.

734
00:28:12,925 --> 00:28:14,460
- Well, have you ever
been through one?

735
00:28:14,493 --> 00:28:16,028
- [Tom Servo] Have
you ever been mellow?

736
00:28:16,062 --> 00:28:17,230
- Only the fringes.

737
00:28:17,263 --> 00:28:18,998
- Well, this one's
building up very fast,

738
00:28:19,032 --> 00:28:21,067
pressure dropped very
quickly in the center.

739
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:22,535
I'd advise you to get
some doors and windows

740
00:28:22,568 --> 00:28:23,703
open in this place.

741
00:28:23,737 --> 00:28:25,605
- Yes, Mr. Ventilation.

742
00:28:27,507 --> 00:28:29,575
- Ventilators on the roof,

743
00:28:29,608 --> 00:28:31,277
and if you'll freshen Ann's
drink, I'll go and check them.

744
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:33,145
- Flesh in man's drink?

745
00:28:33,178 --> 00:28:34,947
- [Tom Servo] I don't get it.

746
00:28:34,980 --> 00:28:37,283
- Thank heavens you arrived.

747
00:28:37,317 --> 00:28:38,518
- Frosty malt?

748
00:28:38,552 --> 00:28:39,785
- Why, rations
are getting short?

749
00:28:39,818 --> 00:28:42,288
- No, it's more than
that, much more.

750
00:28:42,322 --> 00:28:44,923
We'll surely be able to
sail tomorrow, won't we?

751
00:28:44,957 --> 00:28:46,125
- Possibly.

752
00:28:46,158 --> 00:28:48,127
But not probable.

753
00:28:48,160 --> 00:28:49,795
Not til late, anyway.

754
00:28:49,828 --> 00:28:52,032
Takes a long time for a sea
like that to quiet down.

755
00:28:52,065 --> 00:28:54,433
- But if you're worried
about me, you needn't.

756
00:28:54,467 --> 00:28:55,468
I'm a good sailor.

757
00:28:55,502 --> 00:28:58,070
- Aye aye, all hands on deck.

758
00:28:59,672 --> 00:29:01,107
- We'll sail when
the time's right.

759
00:29:01,140 --> 00:29:03,108
- [Marlowe] Got them
opened all right.

760
00:29:03,142 --> 00:29:05,645
- [Tom Servo] That's
great, now close them up.

761
00:29:05,678 --> 00:29:07,780
- Well captain, let
me freshen your drink.

762
00:29:07,813 --> 00:29:08,682
- [Tom Servo and Joel]
Flesh in your drink?

763
00:29:08,715 --> 00:29:10,350
- [Joel] That's what he said.

764
00:29:10,383 --> 00:29:11,650
- Not trying to rush you, but--

765
00:29:11,683 --> 00:29:13,118
- Get out, get out!

766
00:29:13,152 --> 00:29:15,755
- I've invited Thorne
for dinner, father.

767
00:29:15,788 --> 00:29:17,190
- [Joel] Does anybody
know the plot yet?

768
00:29:17,223 --> 00:29:18,958
- Oh, I see.

769
00:29:18,992 --> 00:29:21,293
- [Joel] London, I see France.

770
00:29:21,327 --> 00:29:24,597
- If you're not worried about
your ship, you're welcome.

771
00:29:24,630 --> 00:29:26,298
- I'll take a rain
check on that dinner.

772
00:29:26,332 --> 00:29:27,533
- If you wish.

773
00:29:27,567 --> 00:29:30,102
- Father, I've asked
Thorne to stay.

774
00:29:30,137 --> 00:29:32,005
- Hey everybody, what
does this remind you of?

775
00:29:32,038 --> 00:29:36,008
- [Joel] He's a brilliant
man, but he saves his phlegm.

776
00:29:36,977 --> 00:29:38,978
- Sole survivor of group 30.

777
00:29:39,012 --> 00:29:40,980
28 months old today.

778
00:29:41,013 --> 00:29:45,083
♪ Happy birthday to you

779
00:29:45,117 --> 00:29:47,387
- That's right,
yet still maintains

780
00:29:47,420 --> 00:29:50,723
low metabolism without
any sluggishness.

781
00:29:50,757 --> 00:29:52,458
- [Joel] He's the guy who
taught LBJ how to hold dogs.

782
00:29:52,492 --> 00:29:54,960
- It certainly sets our course.

783
00:29:56,095 --> 00:29:58,965
- Radford, suspend series 52--

784
00:29:58,998 --> 00:30:00,300
- [Joel] Ratford?

785
00:30:00,333 --> 00:30:03,102
- What the heck is
he talking about?

786
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:04,003
- What is that?

787
00:30:04,037 --> 00:30:06,105
- It's a sorex soricidae.

788
00:30:06,138 --> 00:30:07,407
- [Tom Servo] But
I call him Rick.

789
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:08,975
- Looks like a small rat.

790
00:30:09,008 --> 00:30:10,977
Smells like a skunk.

791
00:30:11,010 --> 00:30:13,012
- [Joel] Looks delicious.

792
00:30:13,045 --> 00:30:17,050
- These little fellas
are our subjects.

793
00:30:17,117 --> 00:30:20,553
They have a birth
cycle of 10 to 14 days,

794
00:30:20,587 --> 00:30:22,955
and using them we
can establish traits.

795
00:30:22,988 --> 00:30:25,258
- This guy makes Al
Louis look handsome.

796
00:30:25,292 --> 00:30:27,927
- Over a short period of time.

797
00:30:27,960 --> 00:30:29,528
- Well, how big do they get?

798
00:30:29,562 --> 00:30:30,930
(dramatic music)

799
00:30:30,963 --> 00:30:32,432
- How big does that
music make it sound?

800
00:30:32,465 --> 00:30:34,067
- That's an adult.

801
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:36,435
- I've got a big, dirty secret.

802
00:30:36,468 --> 00:30:38,638
- See, the muzzle is longer
and thicker than the rats.

803
00:30:38,672 --> 00:30:39,972
- [Tom Servo] Thicker?

804
00:30:40,005 --> 00:30:41,107
- It extends over the
lower mandible, see?

805
00:30:41,140 --> 00:30:43,308
- [Joel] Guys, want to
get back to the movie?

806
00:30:43,342 --> 00:30:44,877
- [Tom Servo] Be nice.

807
00:30:44,910 --> 00:30:46,412
- I can't think of my line.

808
00:30:46,445 --> 00:30:49,882
- All he knows is his next meal.

809
00:30:49,915 --> 00:30:51,918
- [Joel] Which is you.

810
00:30:51,952 --> 00:30:54,053
- He's just been fed.

811
00:30:54,087 --> 00:30:55,855
He'll be alright for
another eight hours.

812
00:30:55,888 --> 00:30:57,023
(loud banging)

813
00:30:57,057 --> 00:30:58,023
(Ann screams)

814
00:30:58,057 --> 00:30:59,625
- Honey, switch to decaf.

815
00:30:59,658 --> 00:31:00,860
- A shutter blew open.

816
00:31:00,893 --> 00:31:01,962
Radford.

817
00:31:01,995 --> 00:31:04,430
- I've got it.
- Ow, aw, gee.

818
00:31:05,465 --> 00:31:06,900
- You let that scare you?

819
00:31:06,933 --> 00:31:08,602
- [Tom Servo] Does it bug you?

820
00:31:08,635 --> 00:31:09,968
- Storms have always
frightened her,

821
00:31:10,002 --> 00:31:12,105
ever since she was a child.

822
00:31:13,640 --> 00:31:17,843
(singing tune from
Hawaii Five-O)

823
00:31:21,915 --> 00:31:23,950
They're not climbers.

824
00:31:23,950 --> 00:31:26,852
They are digging animals,
a lot like the mole.

825
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:28,220
- Let me drop it
down your shirt.

826
00:31:28,253 --> 00:31:31,057
- They feed only at night
unless they're starving.

827
00:31:31,090 --> 00:31:32,925
And when they are hungry enough,

828
00:31:32,958 --> 00:31:36,028
they'll tackle anything,
regardless of size.

829
00:31:36,062 --> 00:31:37,830
- [Joel] Like LT,
Lawrence Taylor.

830
00:31:37,863 --> 00:31:40,767
- Keep two of them in a cage
for 12 hours without food,

831
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:42,868
the stronger will
eat the weaker.

832
00:31:42,902 --> 00:31:43,837
- It's fun.

833
00:31:43,870 --> 00:31:46,005
- They're cannibals.
- Precisely.

834
00:31:46,038 --> 00:31:48,007
- [Joel] Don't say cannibal.

835
00:31:48,040 --> 00:31:51,243
- Requires a tremendous
amount of energy.

836
00:31:51,277 --> 00:31:54,880
To supply it, they
must eat three times

837
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:59,085
their own weight in food
every 24 hours, or starve.

838
00:31:59,118 --> 00:32:00,853
- Guys, guys, that was
covered in the voiceover

839
00:32:00,887 --> 00:32:03,255
at the beginning of the movie.

840
00:32:04,823 --> 00:32:06,558
- [Joel] Alright, I want you
to pick a card, any card,

841
00:32:06,592 --> 00:32:10,897
out of the middle of
the deck is fine now.

842
00:32:10,930 --> 00:32:12,998
- Some call them bone eaters.

843
00:32:13,032 --> 00:32:14,533
- I call them cheddarwurst.

844
00:32:14,567 --> 00:32:16,568
- When the flesh is
gone, they'll eat
the bones for marrow.

845
00:32:16,602 --> 00:32:19,738
All they'll leave are
teeth, horns, hooves--

846
00:32:19,772 --> 00:32:21,975
- I could use another
martini, do you mind?

847
00:32:22,008 --> 00:32:23,475
- Of course, my dear.

848
00:32:23,508 --> 00:32:24,810
I'll get you one.

849
00:32:26,145 --> 00:32:29,282
- You don't pick
your family, do you?

850
00:32:29,282 --> 00:32:32,285
- Just humor him,
he's not well, hi.

851
00:32:33,152 --> 00:32:34,553
- There you are.

852
00:32:35,688 --> 00:32:36,755
- [Tom Servo] Drink it down.

853
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:38,190
- Mario.

854
00:32:38,223 --> 00:32:39,425
Mario!

855
00:32:39,458 --> 00:32:40,827
- Yes, Mr. Beatty.

856
00:32:42,695 --> 00:32:44,263
- Mario will show
you to the bath,

857
00:32:44,297 --> 00:32:45,798
you will freshen up a bit.

858
00:32:45,832 --> 00:32:50,002
(speaking in foreign language)

859
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:54,140
- Hit him with the bathroom?

860
00:32:56,842 --> 00:33:00,012
- Oh Nita, what are
you trying to prove?

861
00:33:00,045 --> 00:33:02,382
- [Joel] Finish your drink.

862
00:33:05,885 --> 00:33:07,787
Well, listen, here's
the caveman room.

863
00:33:07,820 --> 00:33:09,988
You'll really enjoy it.

864
00:33:10,022 --> 00:33:11,623
- Turtle Bulkowski
was here before you,

865
00:33:11,657 --> 00:33:12,992
sorry about the mess.

866
00:33:13,025 --> 00:33:16,695
- The martini faucet's in
back, oh, you found it.

867
00:33:16,728 --> 00:33:19,632
- Oh, strip over the toilet,
sanitized for my protection.

868
00:33:19,665 --> 00:33:22,735
- Is your room comfortable, sir?

869
00:33:22,768 --> 00:33:25,003
Can I unpack your hat?

870
00:33:25,037 --> 00:33:29,608
- [Joel] Uh, please don't
drink from the bidet.

871
00:33:29,642 --> 00:33:31,610
- You got a problem, too?

872
00:33:31,643 --> 00:33:32,812
Que paso?

873
00:33:32,845 --> 00:33:35,013
- Nada, nothing, senor.

874
00:33:35,047 --> 00:33:38,117
But you will leave
on the ship tomorrow.

875
00:33:38,150 --> 00:33:39,485
- Well, I think that all depends

876
00:33:39,518 --> 00:33:41,587
on the wind and
the sea, don't you?

877
00:33:41,620 --> 00:33:42,888
- Si.

878
00:33:42,922 --> 00:33:45,090
- [Joel] Regular Walt
Whitman, aren't you?

879
00:33:45,123 --> 00:33:46,458
- I don't know.

880
00:33:47,627 --> 00:33:50,630
Ah, you're joking.
(laughing)

881
00:33:50,663 --> 00:33:51,463
I see it, boy.

882
00:33:51,497 --> 00:33:52,932
I see.

883
00:33:52,965 --> 00:33:55,267
- Well, I'm glad to hear that.

884
00:33:55,300 --> 00:33:57,637
If anybody else is concerned
about my sailing tomorrow

885
00:33:57,670 --> 00:34:00,005
why, you see they feel
the point too, huh?

886
00:34:00,038 --> 00:34:00,973
- Ouch.
- I don't like

887
00:34:01,007 --> 00:34:02,508
repeating myself.

888
00:34:02,542 --> 00:34:03,743
- Okay, Senor.

889
00:34:03,777 --> 00:34:06,212
(upbeat music)

890
00:34:09,148 --> 00:34:11,583
(whooshing)

891
00:34:13,518 --> 00:34:17,490
- [Joel] Oh, he's got to plug
in the boat for the night.

892
00:34:17,523 --> 00:34:20,893
Aw, someone left the
cake out in the rain.

893
00:34:22,995 --> 00:34:25,998
- [Tom Servo] What's
he doing there?

894
00:34:27,167 --> 00:34:28,200
Oh, I get it!

895
00:34:28,233 --> 00:34:30,135
This is Knot's Landing!

896
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:37,710
- I know, but I'm not saying
that you created them.

897
00:34:37,743 --> 00:34:40,447
I am saying that because
of your drunken stupidity

898
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:41,980
in leaving the cage door open,

899
00:34:42,013 --> 00:34:45,050
you created the horrible
situation that now exists.

900
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,352
- [Tom Servo] Now, Miss Kitty--

901
00:34:46,385 --> 00:34:49,788
- Like any one of
us might have made.

902
00:34:49,822 --> 00:34:51,690
I'm getting a little
sick of being called

903
00:34:51,723 --> 00:34:54,427
an irresponsible drunk.
(Joel coughing)

904
00:34:54,460 --> 00:34:56,795
Now believe me, I am.

905
00:34:56,828 --> 00:34:58,097
- [Tom Servo] Hi, is
the irresponsible drunk,

906
00:34:58,130 --> 00:35:00,065
oh, there you are!

907
00:35:00,098 --> 00:35:01,267
- Excuse me.

908
00:35:01,300 --> 00:35:04,937
- [Tom Servo] Two people
per scene, please.

909
00:35:04,970 --> 00:35:06,605
- [Joel] All right, I'm leaving,

910
00:35:06,638 --> 00:35:09,608
and as soon as I close the
door, I'm gone, all right?

911
00:35:09,642 --> 00:35:10,442
So, shrew?

912
00:35:13,145 --> 00:35:14,380
- Care for a cigarette?

913
00:35:14,413 --> 00:35:15,213
- [Tom Servo] Why, thank you.

914
00:35:15,213 --> 00:35:16,415
I have emphysema.

915
00:35:16,482 --> 00:35:17,417
- Thank heavens
you arrived today.

916
00:35:17,450 --> 00:35:18,350
- You said that before.

917
00:35:18,383 --> 00:35:19,818
What's the strain?

918
00:35:19,852 --> 00:35:21,187
- [Ann] I don't understand.

919
00:35:21,220 --> 00:35:25,692
- [Tom Servo] Aw, nuts, I got
my shirt caught in the door.

920
00:35:25,725 --> 00:35:28,660
- I want to leave, but I
want my father to go with me.

921
00:35:28,693 --> 00:35:30,863
- Well then, why doesn't he?

922
00:35:33,132 --> 00:35:35,502
- We've discussed it many
times, but he's adamant.

923
00:35:35,535 --> 00:35:36,402
- [Tom Servo] Oh, he's Adam Ant.

924
00:35:36,435 --> 00:35:37,770
I didn't know.

925
00:35:37,803 --> 00:35:39,738
- I'm sure Jerry has a lot
to do with his decision.

926
00:35:39,772 --> 00:35:40,940
- [Tom Servo] Now
who's this Jerry the,

927
00:35:40,973 --> 00:35:42,608
oh, I'm Jerry.

928
00:35:42,642 --> 00:35:44,510
- Had to convince me that
the crisis will only last

929
00:35:44,543 --> 00:35:46,112
for a few--
- Oh, hi.

930
00:35:47,380 --> 00:35:48,882
- [Joel] What?

931
00:35:48,915 --> 00:35:49,915
Oh, you see, I forgot my thing,

932
00:35:49,982 --> 00:35:52,252
and, huh, I need it for
this thing I'm doing.

933
00:35:52,285 --> 00:35:54,353
- This is certainly
a cozy little scene.

934
00:35:54,387 --> 00:35:56,355
- [Tom Servo] It
was gonna be cozy.

935
00:35:56,388 --> 00:35:57,657
- Might even be called intimate.

936
00:35:57,690 --> 00:36:00,258
Boy meets girl--
- Stop it, Jer.

937
00:36:00,292 --> 00:36:04,097
What I do or have to say
does not concern you.

938
00:36:05,230 --> 00:36:07,233
- I can't disagree
with you more, my dear.

939
00:36:07,267 --> 00:36:08,700
I'm concerned with
everything you do

940
00:36:08,733 --> 00:36:09,768
and I intend to
keep it that way.

941
00:36:09,802 --> 00:36:11,103
- [Joel] I'm outta here.

942
00:36:11,137 --> 00:36:13,438
- Now, in my book an engagement
isn't a casual thing.

943
00:36:13,438 --> 00:36:15,040
- In my book it isn't either.

944
00:36:15,073 --> 00:36:17,310
And last night ended ours.

945
00:36:17,343 --> 00:36:19,745
(wind whooshing)

946
00:36:19,778 --> 00:36:22,548
- [Tom Servo] Dorothy, Dorothy!

947
00:36:26,052 --> 00:36:28,787
- Hey, that sounds like
a Dixieland jazz band.

948
00:36:28,820 --> 00:36:30,690
- Now he's doing it.
- Oh, stop it!

949
00:36:30,723 --> 00:36:33,792
(wind whooshing)
- Careful.

950
00:36:33,825 --> 00:36:35,027
Cute little gun.

951
00:36:35,060 --> 00:36:35,995
Puppies!

952
00:36:36,028 --> 00:36:39,498
- Oh, yeah.
(gunshots)

953
00:36:39,532 --> 00:36:40,532
- [Tom Servo] Sit, stay!

954
00:36:40,567 --> 00:36:41,467
Sit, oh, you stay!

955
00:36:41,500 --> 00:36:43,302
You stay, you stay, you stay!

956
00:36:43,335 --> 00:36:47,840
Sit! (smooching)
(thunder rumbling)

957
00:36:47,873 --> 00:36:49,208
- [Tom Servo] Oh, will ya
look at those pants go?

958
00:36:49,242 --> 00:36:51,843
- Kinda feels good, mmm.

959
00:36:51,877 --> 00:36:54,047
(suspenseful music)
- Uh-oh.

960
00:36:54,080 --> 00:36:55,247
- [Tom Servo] Uh-oh, big dog!

961
00:36:55,280 --> 00:36:57,850
Oh, run! (sputtering)

962
00:36:57,883 --> 00:37:00,820
(thunder rumbling)
(suspenseful music)

963
00:37:00,853 --> 00:37:01,620
Hmm.

964
00:37:01,653 --> 00:37:04,723
(Tom Servo babbling)

965
00:37:05,925 --> 00:37:07,225
- Gee, they're just puppies.

966
00:37:07,260 --> 00:37:09,028
What's he running
from puppies for?

967
00:37:09,062 --> 00:37:10,630
- [Joel] Hi there,
I'm Kurt Dowdy.

968
00:37:10,630 --> 00:37:12,665
We're out hunting with George
Kirby from Big Texas Shrew

969
00:37:12,698 --> 00:37:15,702
and it's really not
going that well.

970
00:37:15,735 --> 00:37:18,703
- [Tom Servo] Ren, Stimpy, no!

971
00:37:18,737 --> 00:37:19,505
- Help, help!

972
00:37:19,538 --> 00:37:20,707
Captain Thorne!

973
00:37:20,740 --> 00:37:21,507
Somebody help!
- Go away, go away!

974
00:37:21,540 --> 00:37:23,275
I'll help you.

975
00:37:23,308 --> 00:37:25,177
- [Tom Servo] Hey, just
throw us your wallet.

976
00:37:25,210 --> 00:37:28,180
(thunder rumbling)

977
00:37:28,213 --> 00:37:30,650
Wait 'til I finish my Saratoga.

978
00:37:31,883 --> 00:37:33,452
- Be reasonable.

979
00:37:33,485 --> 00:37:35,755
Everybody in the world is
scared to death of something.

980
00:37:35,788 --> 00:37:36,922
- That's evident.

981
00:37:36,955 --> 00:37:38,457
When they came at us last night,

982
00:37:38,490 --> 00:37:40,592
you knocked me down
getting inside the fence.

983
00:37:40,627 --> 00:37:42,193
- It's just that I
can't stand them.

984
00:37:42,227 --> 00:37:44,497
- Oh, now I've discovered
something I can't stand.

985
00:37:44,530 --> 00:37:45,430
- Spackle.

986
00:37:45,463 --> 00:37:46,198
It bugs me.

987
00:37:46,232 --> 00:37:47,500
- All right.

988
00:37:47,533 --> 00:37:49,802
But I advise you not to
mention it to anyone.

989
00:37:49,835 --> 00:37:51,170
- [Tom Servo] And don't
leave the country.

990
00:37:51,203 --> 00:37:52,705
- I'm gonna complete these
experiments with your father

991
00:37:52,738 --> 00:37:54,807
regardless of anything,
do you understand that?

992
00:37:54,840 --> 00:37:56,808
Nobody is gonna take
this chance away from me.

993
00:37:56,842 --> 00:38:00,545
- [Tom Servo] Your
breath smells like feet!

994
00:38:01,380 --> 00:38:03,115
- Where's Captain Sherman?

995
00:38:03,148 --> 00:38:04,017
- Checking the weather.

996
00:38:04,050 --> 00:38:05,685
I'll get him.

997
00:38:05,718 --> 00:38:08,620
(Joel humming)

998
00:38:08,653 --> 00:38:09,988
(exclaiming)

999
00:38:10,022 --> 00:38:11,490
- [Ann] Captain,
time for dinner.

1000
00:38:11,523 --> 00:38:12,592
- [Joel] Man, it's
really breezy in my room.

1001
00:38:12,625 --> 00:38:13,725
- [Tom Servo] We're
having tobacco salad

1002
00:38:13,758 --> 00:38:16,628
with a light gin dressing.

1003
00:38:16,662 --> 00:38:18,297
- Meanwhile, back at the branch.

1004
00:38:18,330 --> 00:38:19,098
- [Tom Servo] D'oh!

1005
00:38:19,132 --> 00:38:20,298
- Help!

1006
00:38:20,332 --> 00:38:20,900
Somebody, help!
- Hang in there, baby.

1007
00:38:20,933 --> 00:38:22,133
Friday's coming.

1008
00:38:23,102 --> 00:38:25,772
(shrews screeching)
- Ooh.

1009
00:38:25,805 --> 00:38:27,773
You know, this is another
one of those scenes

1010
00:38:27,807 --> 00:38:30,743
that is so offensive
on so many levels.

1011
00:38:30,777 --> 00:38:32,010
- [Tom Servo] I hear ya.

1012
00:38:32,043 --> 00:38:34,180
- [Tom Servo] Uh-oh,
he's shooting the ground!

1013
00:38:34,213 --> 00:38:38,250
- [Tom Servo] A little
Roscoe for ya, shew!

1014
00:38:38,283 --> 00:38:39,585
(Rook screaming)

1015
00:38:39,618 --> 00:38:41,153
- D'oh, they're
licking me, stop it!

1016
00:38:41,187 --> 00:38:43,388
No, stop it, cut
it out! (laughing)

1017
00:38:43,422 --> 00:38:44,723
Oh, it tickles!

1018
00:38:44,757 --> 00:38:45,590
- [Tom Servo] They're
licking him to death.

1019
00:38:45,623 --> 00:38:47,893
How cute! (laughing)

1020
00:38:47,927 --> 00:38:49,728
(shrews screeching)

1021
00:38:49,762 --> 00:38:52,030
- I'm shakin' the bush, boss.

1022
00:38:53,498 --> 00:38:55,333
(suspenseful music)
(shrews screeching)

1023
00:38:55,367 --> 00:38:56,268
- Hmm.
(thunder rumbling)

1024
00:38:56,302 --> 00:38:57,837
- [Joel] Ooh, he exploded!

1025
00:38:57,870 --> 00:38:59,138
Hmm.

1026
00:38:59,172 --> 00:39:01,173
- I hate the smell of wet shrew.

1027
00:39:01,207 --> 00:39:02,608
(rumbling)

1028
00:39:02,642 --> 00:39:04,243
- [Tom Servo] Are the
dogs and shrews friends?

1029
00:39:04,277 --> 00:39:06,678
Is that what's going on?

1030
00:39:06,712 --> 00:39:08,013
(Ann gasping)
(explosion)

1031
00:39:08,047 --> 00:39:09,182
- [Joel] I think I just
heard Griswald explode.

1032
00:39:09,248 --> 00:39:09,948
You?
- A miss is as good as a mile,

1033
00:39:09,982 --> 00:39:11,517
I always say.

1034
00:39:11,550 --> 00:39:12,718
- You know, if one of those
trees crashes through,

1035
00:39:12,752 --> 00:39:14,353
it might just knock the whole--

1036
00:39:14,387 --> 00:39:15,620
- Look, honey, any tree
on this side of the house

1037
00:39:15,653 --> 00:39:16,855
will fall away from
it, so just relax.

1038
00:39:16,888 --> 00:39:18,423
- [Tom Servo] Oh, you're
a tree surgeon now?

1039
00:39:18,457 --> 00:39:20,860
- I think I'd better
go back aboard.

1040
00:39:20,893 --> 00:39:22,862
Oh, don't think I'm not
grateful for your hospitality.

1041
00:39:22,895 --> 00:39:24,930
I am.
- But you're out of liquor so.

1042
00:39:24,963 --> 00:39:27,232
- Your ship is safe.

1043
00:39:27,265 --> 00:39:29,902
Please, stay here with me.

1044
00:39:29,935 --> 00:39:31,537
- [Joel] Is there
somebody under that dress?

1045
00:39:31,570 --> 00:39:33,305
- Are you scared or lonesome?

1046
00:39:33,338 --> 00:39:35,573
- [Tom Servo] Chicken,
chicken. (bawking)

1047
00:39:35,607 --> 00:39:37,042
- I'll take a rain check on it.

1048
00:39:37,075 --> 00:39:39,645
- Thorne, you can't leave.

1049
00:39:39,678 --> 00:39:43,048
No one opens that
gate after dark.

1050
00:39:43,048 --> 00:39:45,683
- Well, who's
gonna stop me, you?

1051
00:39:45,717 --> 00:39:47,018
- How about this?

1052
00:39:47,052 --> 00:39:48,220
- [Joel] How about
my friend, Roscoe?

1053
00:39:48,253 --> 00:39:49,422
- No one opens
that gate at night.

1054
00:39:49,455 --> 00:39:51,957
(thunder rumbling)

1055
00:39:51,990 --> 00:39:53,392
- [Tom Servo] Open that
gate, come on, Robin!

1056
00:39:53,425 --> 00:39:54,527
Open that gate!

1057
00:39:54,560 --> 00:39:55,727
- Now, look, I
don't ask questions

1058
00:39:55,762 --> 00:39:57,195
because it's against
my principles.

1059
00:39:57,228 --> 00:39:58,563
- [Tom Servo] Your what?

1060
00:39:58,597 --> 00:40:00,432
- Wouldn't you like
to explain that?

1061
00:40:00,465 --> 00:40:02,568
- [Joel] Well, you see,
the hammer hits the primer

1062
00:40:02,602 --> 00:40:04,270
and the primer--
- Give me the gun.

1063
00:40:04,303 --> 00:40:06,872
Not very becoming anyway.
- Oh, rats.

1064
00:40:06,905 --> 00:40:08,240
- You believe in fairy tales?

1065
00:40:08,273 --> 00:40:09,908
- [Tom Servo] Does
it got elves in it?

1066
00:40:09,942 --> 00:40:11,777
- Well, I'm a little old
for that sort of thing,

1067
00:40:11,810 --> 00:40:13,545
but what'd you have in mind?

1068
00:40:13,578 --> 00:40:15,580
- Well, I'll tell you about one.

1069
00:40:15,613 --> 00:40:18,383
A true fairy tale, and you
arrived in the middle of it.

1070
00:40:18,417 --> 00:40:19,218
- Oh?

1071
00:40:20,385 --> 00:40:21,687
- [Ann] Have you ever
heard of a shrew?

1072
00:40:21,720 --> 00:40:24,523
- As in Taming of the--
- No, the animal.

1073
00:40:24,557 --> 00:40:26,858
Radford called them
sorex soricidae when
he showed you one.

1074
00:40:26,892 --> 00:40:29,662
- Oh, then shrew must
be the common name

1075
00:40:29,695 --> 00:40:31,030
for those cute little animals.

1076
00:40:31,063 --> 00:40:32,330
- Cute?
- No, they're adorable.

1077
00:40:32,363 --> 00:40:33,232
- That's the last
word you can use

1078
00:40:33,265 --> 00:40:35,233
to describe those monsters.

1079
00:40:35,267 --> 00:40:38,437
They're the most
horrible animals on
the face of the earth.

1080
00:40:38,470 --> 00:40:39,238
- A murderer?

1081
00:40:39,272 --> 00:40:40,505
- My father told you,

1082
00:40:40,538 --> 00:40:41,573
they breed within three
weeks after birth.

1083
00:40:41,607 --> 00:40:43,075
Their lifespan is
around one year.

1084
00:40:43,108 --> 00:40:44,543
- Yeah, I know what
your father told me,

1085
00:40:44,577 --> 00:40:47,547
but what's that got to do
with me opening that gate?

1086
00:40:47,580 --> 00:40:48,847
- Pick another category, please.

1087
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:50,148
Still your turn.

1088
00:40:50,215 --> 00:40:52,752
- There are 200 or 300
giant shrews out there.

1089
00:40:52,785 --> 00:40:54,353
- [Joel] Not counting
the dogs, right?

1090
00:40:54,387 --> 00:40:57,022
- Monsters weighing
between 50 and 100 pounds.

1091
00:40:57,055 --> 00:40:59,392
- [Tom Servo] How
did she weigh 'em?

1092
00:40:59,425 --> 00:41:01,660
- 50 to 100 pounds?
- Pounds?

1093
00:41:01,693 --> 00:41:03,528
- Wait a minute,
you must be kidding.

1094
00:41:03,562 --> 00:41:05,797
- I am definitely not kidding.

1095
00:41:05,832 --> 00:41:07,500
- [Tom Servo] I'm
not pulling your leg.

1096
00:41:07,533 --> 00:41:09,133
- [Thorne] That's as big
as a full-grown wolf.

1097
00:41:09,168 --> 00:41:12,572
- And what's more, they
are beginning to starve.

1098
00:41:12,605 --> 00:41:16,608
- [Joel] She's got a real
Hawaii 5-0 hairdo there.

1099
00:41:16,642 --> 00:41:18,510
- No wonder you didn't
want me to go out there.

1100
00:41:18,543 --> 00:41:21,180
Thanks for saving my skin.

1101
00:41:21,213 --> 00:41:23,982
- Well, I'm sorry I had to
threaten you with a gun.

1102
00:41:24,048 --> 00:41:25,650
But I didn't know
how else to stop you.

1103
00:41:25,683 --> 00:41:27,953
- No, it was very effective.
- Quite a turn-on.

1104
00:41:27,987 --> 00:41:29,955
- All you had to do
was tell me about--

1105
00:41:29,988 --> 00:41:31,823
- What is this,
fill in the blank?

1106
00:41:31,857 --> 00:41:34,993
- But you changed everything
when you started to leave,

1107
00:41:35,027 --> 00:41:36,862
and I had to stop you some way.

1108
00:41:36,895 --> 00:41:38,597
- [Joel] I would've been alone.

1109
00:41:38,630 --> 00:41:39,598
I'd rather kill
you than be alone.

1110
00:41:39,632 --> 00:41:41,267
- You say there's
200 or 300 out there?

1111
00:41:41,300 --> 00:41:42,300
- [Tom Servo] Where'd
they get our address?

1112
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:43,135
- Ann.

1113
00:41:44,737 --> 00:41:48,440
- [Tom Servo] Well,
now, Matthew, I sure
could use a gimlet.

1114
00:41:48,473 --> 00:41:50,442
- That's right, Captain Thorne.

1115
00:41:50,475 --> 00:41:52,545
And if you'd stuck with your
rowboat and played captain

1116
00:41:52,578 --> 00:41:54,647
instead of trying
to play detective,

1117
00:41:54,680 --> 00:41:55,713
you wouldn't have to worry about

1118
00:41:55,747 --> 00:41:57,148
how many are out
there, would you?

1119
00:41:57,182 --> 00:41:58,517
- [Dr. Craigis]
That's enough, Jerry.

1120
00:41:58,550 --> 00:41:59,852
- That's a pretty complex
insult for a drunk.

1121
00:41:59,885 --> 00:42:01,320
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

1122
00:42:02,487 --> 00:42:04,757
Oh, now it's like an
Agatha Christie novel, hmm?

1123
00:42:04,790 --> 00:42:05,958
- [Dr. Craigis]
What's wrong, Ann?

1124
00:42:05,992 --> 00:42:07,727
- Mr. Thorne decided to leave.

1125
00:42:07,760 --> 00:42:10,795
To dissuade him I started to
tell him about the shrews.

1126
00:42:10,828 --> 00:42:13,165
- [Tom Servo] Shoes, what
about, oh, shrews, oh!

1127
00:42:13,198 --> 00:42:14,132
- [Dr. Craigis] You might
as well know the whole story

1128
00:42:14,165 --> 00:42:15,433
as half of it.
- For story?

1129
00:42:15,467 --> 00:42:18,403
- [Joel] Doesn't anybody
think about Griswald?

1130
00:42:18,437 --> 00:42:20,838
- [Tom Servo] I've
heard this one before.

1131
00:42:20,872 --> 00:42:22,575
- [Dr. Craigis] I guess we're
all a little jumpy, Captain.

1132
00:42:22,608 --> 00:42:24,310
- Yeah, I'm sorry.

1133
00:42:24,343 --> 00:42:26,612
- [Joel] You're about to
light the filter, Captain.

1134
00:42:26,645 --> 00:42:28,513
- Six months ago we
managed to isolate

1135
00:42:28,547 --> 00:42:30,415
the factor controlling size.

1136
00:42:30,415 --> 00:42:31,383
- [Joel] Ah, what
a night that was.

1137
00:42:31,417 --> 00:42:32,752
- Two litters were born.

1138
00:42:32,785 --> 00:42:34,953
Six individuals kept for study.

1139
00:42:34,987 --> 00:42:36,555
- [Joel] A prosthetic?

1140
00:42:36,588 --> 00:42:38,723
- They were about the
size of buckshot at birth.

1141
00:42:38,757 --> 00:42:40,625
- Hey, he's tall.
- But the rate of growth

1142
00:42:40,658 --> 00:42:44,397
was abnormal.
- I'm on the edge of my chair.

1143
00:42:44,430 --> 00:42:45,630
- They continued to grow, grow.

1144
00:42:45,663 --> 00:42:47,967
- Whoa.
- They were mutants.

1145
00:42:49,468 --> 00:42:51,303
- Jailbreak tonight!

1146
00:42:52,170 --> 00:42:54,507
Everyone through the wire!

1147
00:42:54,540 --> 00:42:58,477
- [Dr. Craigis] Somehow
they managed to escape.

1148
00:43:00,345 --> 00:43:02,815
(upbeat music)

1149
00:43:06,418 --> 00:43:07,385
- One, two.

1150
00:43:07,418 --> 00:43:08,887
- One, two, three, four.

1151
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:10,222
♪ Killer shrew

1152
00:43:10,255 --> 00:43:11,457
♪ Killer shrew

1153
00:43:11,490 --> 00:43:13,558
♪ Don't know the diff
between me and you

1154
00:43:13,592 --> 00:43:14,460
♪ It comes on at night

1155
00:43:14,493 --> 00:43:15,793
♪ To give you a fright

1156
00:43:15,827 --> 00:43:18,297
♪ Don't look now but
he's gonna take a bite

1157
00:43:18,330 --> 00:43:19,298
♪ Da da da da

1158
00:43:19,332 --> 00:43:20,365
♪ Da da da da da da-da-da

1159
00:43:20,398 --> 00:43:21,567
♪ Killer shrew

1160
00:43:21,600 --> 00:43:22,433
♪ Killer shrew

1161
00:43:22,467 --> 00:43:24,770
♪ K-I-Double L-E-R shrew

1162
00:43:24,803 --> 00:43:26,038
♪ He's scary and tall

1163
00:43:26,072 --> 00:43:27,272
♪ If that's not enough

1164
00:43:27,305 --> 00:43:29,775
♪ He's augmented with
bad man and stuff

1165
00:43:29,808 --> 00:43:30,642
♪ Killer shrew

1166
00:43:30,675 --> 00:43:31,943
♪ Killer shrew

1167
00:43:31,977 --> 00:43:34,145
♪ He's coming to
your town to get you

1168
00:43:34,178 --> 00:43:35,380
- Killer shrew, by Marx.

1169
00:43:35,413 --> 00:43:36,482
- All right!

1170
00:43:36,482 --> 00:43:38,250
That was great!

1171
00:43:38,283 --> 00:43:39,885
- Okay, well, consumer Joel.

1172
00:43:39,918 --> 00:43:41,387
That's the enticing jingle.

1173
00:43:41,420 --> 00:43:42,755
Now play the
super-fun board game!

1174
00:43:42,788 --> 00:43:44,457
- Wait a minute, you
guys came up with this

1175
00:43:44,490 --> 00:43:45,390
all by yourselves?

1176
00:43:45,423 --> 00:43:47,058
- El posivito, senorito.

1177
00:43:47,092 --> 00:43:48,427
C'mon, let's play.

1178
00:43:48,460 --> 00:43:49,795
You can be the German guy
and I'll pick the card.

1179
00:43:49,828 --> 00:43:50,728
Right over there.

1180
00:43:50,762 --> 00:43:52,530
- All right, okay, gotcha.

1181
00:43:52,563 --> 00:43:55,767
It says, "Contemplate shrews."

1182
00:43:55,800 --> 00:43:57,568
- Okay, that means
you don't move.

1183
00:43:57,602 --> 00:43:59,170
Okay, now I pick one.

1184
00:43:59,203 --> 00:44:00,738
- Okay, I'll do that for you.

1185
00:44:00,772 --> 00:44:01,873
Okay.

1186
00:44:01,907 --> 00:44:03,775
- Okay, have another martini.

1187
00:44:03,808 --> 00:44:07,545
Okey-doke, I'm the girl, so
I'll just move one piece.

1188
00:44:07,578 --> 00:44:10,748
Oh, you see, it's glued
down, and you can't move it.

1189
00:44:10,782 --> 00:44:12,650
It's just like the
movie, nobody moves!

1190
00:44:12,685 --> 00:44:14,553
(Crow and Tom Servo laughing)

1191
00:44:14,587 --> 00:44:17,422
In fact, nobody moves at
all for over 45 minutes!

1192
00:44:17,455 --> 00:44:19,525
It's enough to numb your brain.

1193
00:44:19,558 --> 00:44:21,527
They sit and talk
and nothing happens,

1194
00:44:21,560 --> 00:44:24,430
and then, cripes, Frank Cannon
gets more action than this.

1195
00:44:24,463 --> 00:44:25,330
- Crow--

1196
00:44:25,363 --> 00:44:26,598
- You think something
might happen

1197
00:44:26,632 --> 00:44:28,200
and your spirit soars,
but all that happens

1198
00:44:28,233 --> 00:44:29,402
is the black girl changes
and she's not even that cute!

1199
00:44:29,435 --> 00:44:30,402
- Crow--

1200
00:44:30,435 --> 00:44:32,003
- And the Cuban guy mumbles
- Crow--

1201
00:44:32,037 --> 00:44:33,438
- and so does the Captain
and they all just drink more!

1202
00:44:33,472 --> 00:44:36,608
- I'm scared, I'm scared!
(Crow babbling)

1203
00:44:36,642 --> 00:44:38,943
- Can't tell what this is!

1204
00:44:38,977 --> 00:44:40,512
(Crow and Tom Servo sobbing)

1205
00:44:40,545 --> 00:44:43,348
- Aww, that's okay, that's okay.

1206
00:44:43,348 --> 00:44:47,418
Joel's got you, it's
all right, it's okay.

1207
00:44:47,452 --> 00:44:50,655
No, you guys, you didn't
have to do this for me.

1208
00:44:50,688 --> 00:44:52,490
You're both such troopers,

1209
00:44:52,523 --> 00:44:55,460
in the theater, quippin'
like there's no tomorrow,

1210
00:44:55,493 --> 00:44:59,832
making kooky comments
on contemporary mores.

1211
00:44:59,865 --> 00:45:01,633
You know, making
arcane references

1212
00:45:01,667 --> 00:45:05,203
at the drop of a hat,
I love you little guys!

1213
00:45:05,237 --> 00:45:06,238
- Thanks, Joel.

1214
00:45:06,272 --> 00:45:07,538
We love you too.

1215
00:45:07,572 --> 00:45:09,708
- It's just, you were
so funny in the theater,

1216
00:45:09,742 --> 00:45:13,378
we didn't know if you could
tell this movie was a honk shoe.

1217
00:45:13,412 --> 00:45:14,413
- A honk shoe?

1218
00:45:14,447 --> 00:45:15,713
What's that?

1219
00:45:15,747 --> 00:45:17,715
- Oh, you know, honk
shoe. (imitating snoring)

1220
00:45:17,750 --> 00:45:20,785
(all laughing)

1221
00:45:20,818 --> 00:45:22,353
(all sighing)

1222
00:45:22,387 --> 00:45:24,155
(beeping)
(all exclaiming)

1223
00:45:24,188 --> 00:45:27,392
(clicking, whooshing)

1224
00:45:34,065 --> 00:45:35,067
- About a month later...

1225
00:45:35,100 --> 00:45:37,468
(chattering)

1226
00:45:37,502 --> 00:45:39,137
They were multiplying.

1227
00:45:39,170 --> 00:45:43,008
We did everything in the
world to exterminate them,

1228
00:45:43,042 --> 00:45:45,543
but (scoffing) no apparent luck.

1229
00:45:45,577 --> 00:45:47,145
- [Joel] Did you
try Roach Motel?

1230
00:45:47,178 --> 00:45:50,015
- We haven't seen any,
since daylight blinds them

1231
00:45:50,048 --> 00:45:53,385
and they forage only at
night when they're starving.

1232
00:45:53,418 --> 00:45:55,953
- [Tom Servo] Hmm, he's got
a few hairs left up there.

1233
00:45:55,987 --> 00:45:58,323
- But the fact that two of
them charged Ann and Jerry

1234
00:45:58,357 --> 00:46:01,860
at the gate last
evening indicates

1235
00:46:01,893 --> 00:46:04,162
that the available
food on the island

1236
00:46:04,195 --> 00:46:05,963
is nearing depletion.

1237
00:46:05,997 --> 00:46:08,800
- [Crow] Well, let's
have a food drive!

1238
00:46:08,833 --> 00:46:10,402
- Then what, Doctor?

1239
00:46:11,637 --> 00:46:14,038
- [Tom Servo] That's
it, don't you get it?

1240
00:46:14,072 --> 00:46:15,540
- It will take a couple days.

1241
00:46:15,573 --> 00:46:17,208
- What do we do
during that time?

1242
00:46:17,242 --> 00:46:18,343
- [Joel] Well,
there's always liquor.

1243
00:46:18,377 --> 00:46:20,145
- Stay indoors and
wait until it's over.

1244
00:46:20,178 --> 00:46:21,480
(suspenseful music)

1245
00:46:21,513 --> 00:46:22,380
- [Crow] Oh no!

1246
00:46:22,413 --> 00:46:23,682
They've got wire cutters!

1247
00:46:23,682 --> 00:46:26,318
- [Thorne] I guess some wires
are down on the transom.

1248
00:46:26,352 --> 00:46:28,120
- [Ann] I'm sorry.

1249
00:46:28,153 --> 00:46:31,357
- [Joel] Everyone, quick,
light your martinis!

1250
00:46:31,390 --> 00:46:32,257
- [Jerry] Mario!

1251
00:46:32,290 --> 00:46:33,292
Mario!

1252
00:46:33,325 --> 00:46:35,360
- [Mario] Si, senor?

1253
00:46:35,393 --> 00:46:36,595
- There's a light
in the pack there.

1254
00:46:36,628 --> 00:46:37,495
Light it and bring it in here.

1255
00:46:37,528 --> 00:46:40,465
- [Joel] I'll fix the drinks.

1256
00:46:40,498 --> 00:46:42,868
- [Jerry] Radford, light all
the candles you can find.

1257
00:46:42,902 --> 00:46:43,668
- All right, I will.
- And curse the darkness.

1258
00:46:43,702 --> 00:46:44,937
- [Craigis] Outside.

1259
00:46:44,970 --> 00:46:47,638
Can't get at it at night.

1260
00:46:47,672 --> 00:46:49,207
(suspenseful music)

1261
00:46:49,240 --> 00:46:50,442
- [Tom Servo] She's kind
of wearing fluffy culottes,

1262
00:46:50,475 --> 00:46:52,077
isn't she?
- Mm-hmm.

1263
00:46:52,110 --> 00:46:53,778
- A lantern will give you
all the light you need.

1264
00:46:53,812 --> 00:46:55,480
- [Joel] It's just as
light with candles.

1265
00:46:55,513 --> 00:46:57,382
- [Tom Servo] Hmm, amazing.

1266
00:46:57,448 --> 00:46:59,952
- [Tom Servo] This is
like a bad production

1267
00:46:59,985 --> 00:47:01,353
of a Chekhov play.

1268
00:47:02,487 --> 00:47:04,657
A wild geese.
- I don't like you.

1269
00:47:04,690 --> 00:47:08,293
(thunder rumbling)

1270
00:47:08,327 --> 00:47:10,395
- Well, Jerry, I
felt she was sincere

1271
00:47:10,428 --> 00:47:13,298
and made sense.
- Stop talking

1272
00:47:13,332 --> 00:47:15,133
and finish my pedicure.

1273
00:47:15,167 --> 00:47:16,435
- Wanting her father

1274
00:47:16,468 --> 00:47:17,435
to leave the island
with her makes sense?

1275
00:47:17,468 --> 00:47:19,805
It'd be much better
for the project

1276
00:47:19,838 --> 00:47:23,275
if I went with her
for a few days.

1277
00:47:23,308 --> 00:47:25,010
- [Tom Servo] Maybe
the Fanta suites.

1278
00:47:25,043 --> 00:47:26,678
- As a matter of fact,

1279
00:47:26,712 --> 00:47:28,113
I think I'll talk to
the doctor about that.

1280
00:47:28,147 --> 00:47:29,447
That might be the answer.

1281
00:47:29,480 --> 00:47:30,748
- Oh, great, it'll be a
20-minute scene, I'm sure.

1282
00:47:30,748 --> 00:47:32,717
- I don't think much
of this Thorne Sherman.

1283
00:47:32,750 --> 00:47:35,387
He looks to me like the
type that'd try anything.

1284
00:47:35,420 --> 00:47:36,388
- [Joel] Oh, really?

1285
00:47:36,422 --> 00:47:37,588
I think he's a really nice guy.

1286
00:47:37,622 --> 00:47:39,490
- That left-handed
dinner invitation.

1287
00:47:39,523 --> 00:47:41,593
That was just to keep me here
'til after dark, wasn't it?

1288
00:47:41,627 --> 00:47:43,562
- [Crow] I'm sorry, I was
sure you were left handed.

1289
00:47:43,595 --> 00:47:46,097
Can you eat with either hand?

1290
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:50,235
- I wanted you here tonight.

1291
00:47:50,268 --> 00:47:52,972
I felt something terrible
was going to happen.

1292
00:47:53,005 --> 00:47:54,973
- Well, you still feel
the same way about it?

1293
00:47:55,007 --> 00:47:58,777
- Not as much, not since you're
here and know everything.

1294
00:47:58,810 --> 00:47:59,978
- [Joel] I don't
know everything.

1295
00:48:00,012 --> 00:48:02,713
I don't even know how fish work.

1296
00:48:02,713 --> 00:48:05,183
(suspenseful music)
- Oh, puppy!

1297
00:48:05,217 --> 00:48:06,385
Ooh, cute.

1298
00:48:06,418 --> 00:48:10,055
- No, not Fury!
- The biggest shrew of all.

1299
00:48:12,490 --> 00:48:13,458
- That was weird.

1300
00:48:13,492 --> 00:48:15,627
- I love an open
fire, don't you?

1301
00:48:15,660 --> 00:48:16,862
- Mm-hmm.

1302
00:48:16,895 --> 00:48:18,963
- [Tom Servo] Yeah,
they're great.

1303
00:48:18,997 --> 00:48:20,632
- [Joel] And I
love an open sewer.

1304
00:48:20,665 --> 00:48:23,202
- The wind has the
lonesomest sound.

1305
00:48:23,235 --> 00:48:24,703
Doesn't it?

1306
00:48:24,737 --> 00:48:27,638
- [Tom Servo] Wheat,
nothing but miles of wheat.

1307
00:48:27,672 --> 00:48:30,875
- Back in Sweden we don't
have a wind this strong.

1308
00:48:30,908 --> 00:48:34,478
- [Crow] Tell me
about your home world.

1309
00:48:34,512 --> 00:48:36,348
- You're a strange man, Thorne.

1310
00:48:36,415 --> 00:48:37,315
- [Joel] You're a queer duck.

1311
00:48:37,315 --> 00:48:38,617
- I never met anyone like you.

1312
00:48:38,650 --> 00:48:39,885
- [Thorne] Oh?

1313
00:48:41,152 --> 00:48:43,222
- You seem so disinterested
in everything.

1314
00:48:43,255 --> 00:48:44,522
- [Tom Servo] Uh-huh.

1315
00:48:44,555 --> 00:48:45,790
Look, you bore the
heck out of me.

1316
00:48:45,823 --> 00:48:46,425
- Aren't you the
least bit curious?

1317
00:48:46,458 --> 00:48:48,093
- [Joel] Yellow?

1318
00:48:48,127 --> 00:48:49,928
- Don't you wonder about the
unusual things around here?

1319
00:48:49,962 --> 00:48:51,763
- [Crow] Do you ever wonder
where felt comes from?

1320
00:48:51,797 --> 00:48:52,830
- The guns, the fence?

1321
00:48:52,863 --> 00:48:54,633
The shuttered windows?

1322
00:48:55,767 --> 00:48:57,302
My accent, anything?

1323
00:48:57,335 --> 00:48:59,337
- I'll tell you something.

1324
00:48:59,370 --> 00:49:02,440
I'm only interested in
anything that concerns me,

1325
00:49:02,473 --> 00:49:03,942
then I do something about it.

1326
00:49:03,975 --> 00:49:07,212
(horse neighing)

1327
00:49:07,245 --> 00:49:08,247
- [Joel] Did you
say Frau Blooker?

1328
00:49:08,280 --> 00:49:09,815
- You're gonna stay
with me tomorrow,

1329
00:49:09,882 --> 00:49:13,218
whether your father (horse
whinnying drowns out Thorne).

1330
00:49:14,920 --> 00:49:17,422
- [Tom Servo] He was Mister Ed.

1331
00:49:19,423 --> 00:49:20,692
- [Ann] Thorne, no!

1332
00:49:20,725 --> 00:49:22,027
- [Crow] No, don't
go in the bathroom!

1333
00:49:22,060 --> 00:49:23,862
We don't have a fan in there!

1334
00:49:23,895 --> 00:49:25,397
- [Ann] Out there!

1335
00:49:25,430 --> 00:49:28,433
(suspenseful music)

1336
00:49:30,035 --> 00:49:32,270
- [Tom Servo] Kim Curtis and
Kim Curtis in Double Impact!

1337
00:49:32,303 --> 00:49:33,605
- I couldn't take a chance.

1338
00:49:33,638 --> 00:49:36,007
He's fool enough to!

1339
00:49:36,040 --> 00:49:37,408
- Don't be stupid.

1340
00:49:37,442 --> 00:49:40,245
I had no intentions of going
there and opening that gate.

1341
00:49:40,278 --> 00:49:42,280
- [Joel] Oh, now my
mouth's bleeding, Burt!

1342
00:49:42,313 --> 00:49:44,082
- Did you hear it, Doctor?

1343
00:49:44,082 --> 00:49:45,683
It sounded like a human voice.

1344
00:49:45,717 --> 00:49:47,152
I was thinking of Rook.

1345
00:49:47,185 --> 00:49:48,120
- But the livestock.

1346
00:49:48,153 --> 00:49:49,888
The shrews got into the barn!

1347
00:49:49,922 --> 00:49:53,458
- [Crow] The shoes
got into the barn?

1348
00:49:53,492 --> 00:49:56,127
- [Tom Servo] I better put
some alcohol on this wound.

1349
00:49:56,160 --> 00:49:58,330
(dramatic music)

1350
00:49:58,363 --> 00:50:01,733
- Let me guess, the
shoe's in the bar.

1351
00:50:01,767 --> 00:50:03,968
- What was it, Father?

1352
00:50:04,002 --> 00:50:05,170
- The livestock.

1353
00:50:05,203 --> 00:50:07,238
- [Joel] Live
socks, that's, huh?

1354
00:50:07,272 --> 00:50:08,573
- Mario, don't forget

1355
00:50:08,607 --> 00:50:11,042
to bar those doors.
♪ Booze glorious booze

1356
00:50:11,075 --> 00:50:12,477
- I put them in the barn myself.

1357
00:50:12,510 --> 00:50:14,012
- [Joel] What about
a bar mitzvah?

1358
00:50:14,045 --> 00:50:17,048
- They couldn't get
through the wood doors.

1359
00:50:17,048 --> 00:50:19,183
They dug through the dirt floor.

1360
00:50:19,217 --> 00:50:20,518
- [Thorne] Let me ask
you something, Doctor.

1361
00:50:20,552 --> 00:50:21,787
- [Tom Servo] Where
are the olives?

1362
00:50:21,820 --> 00:50:23,122
- How could you
expose all our lives,

1363
00:50:23,155 --> 00:50:25,257
yourself included, with
those things out there?

1364
00:50:25,290 --> 00:50:26,525
- [Crow] Did he just
become more southern?

1365
00:50:26,558 --> 00:50:27,825
- All you had to do
was get the Coast Guard

1366
00:50:27,892 --> 00:50:29,160
or the Navy to come in
here and burn 'em out.

1367
00:50:29,193 --> 00:50:30,462
- [Tom Servo] Give me that.

1368
00:50:30,495 --> 00:50:32,030
- [Thorne] Those
things got loose.

1369
00:50:32,063 --> 00:50:35,133
- Any unusual experiment
can produce unusual results.

1370
00:50:35,167 --> 00:50:36,167
- [Crow] Hey, that was my drink!

1371
00:50:36,200 --> 00:50:38,537
- That's why I
chose this island.

1372
00:50:38,570 --> 00:50:39,872
It's isolated.

1373
00:50:39,905 --> 00:50:42,207
Miles of open water
in any direction.

1374
00:50:42,240 --> 00:50:44,475
- [Joel] Miles of cliff
in every direction.

1375
00:50:44,508 --> 00:50:46,812
- Our project is
privately financed.

1376
00:50:46,845 --> 00:50:48,147
- [Tom Servo] Here comes
Art Buckwald again.

1377
00:50:48,180 --> 00:50:51,115
- Not a product for the
government or military.

1378
00:50:51,148 --> 00:50:52,483
And the world is in no danger.

1379
00:50:52,517 --> 00:50:54,052
- [Crow] Oh, I've been
going through the script

1380
00:50:54,085 --> 00:50:56,053
and I think I'm in this scene.

1381
00:50:56,087 --> 00:50:57,822
- This species does not swim.

1382
00:50:57,855 --> 00:50:59,657
- [Joel] Yes, fishes do swim.

1383
00:50:59,690 --> 00:51:02,193
- This island is their world.

1384
00:51:03,262 --> 00:51:04,963
- [Tom Servo] And welcome to it.

1385
00:51:04,997 --> 00:51:07,265
- Very soon, right
here on this island.

1386
00:51:07,298 --> 00:51:08,900
- [Crow] Appearing
will be Don Ball!

1387
00:51:08,933 --> 00:51:11,470
- Miniature reproduction
of an overpopulated world.

1388
00:51:11,503 --> 00:51:13,003
- [Joel] That'll
bring in the tourists.

1389
00:51:13,037 --> 00:51:14,105
- You will see the importance

1390
00:51:14,138 --> 00:51:16,173
of what we're working to avoid.

1391
00:51:16,207 --> 00:51:18,177
- I'm not concerned
about all this theory.

1392
00:51:18,210 --> 00:51:19,845
What I'm concerned
about is our lives!

1393
00:51:19,878 --> 00:51:21,245
- [Joel] And my Rob Roy.

1394
00:51:21,278 --> 00:51:22,513
- Yeah, well, time to panic
when they run out of food

1395
00:51:22,547 --> 00:51:24,215
and go on a 24-hour forage.

1396
00:51:24,282 --> 00:51:26,818
- How do you know
they haven't already?

1397
00:51:26,852 --> 00:51:30,655
- [Joel] Yes, say yes
to making Martini Rossi.

1398
00:51:32,090 --> 00:51:33,958
- That source could've
been depleted.

1399
00:51:33,992 --> 00:51:35,160
- [Joel] Well, we
need more brandy.

1400
00:51:35,193 --> 00:51:37,228
Need more scotch.

1401
00:51:37,262 --> 00:51:38,297
We're out of vanilla extract.

1402
00:51:38,330 --> 00:51:41,165
- There's still some
food on this island

1403
00:51:41,198 --> 00:51:43,602
before there's a crisis.
- Gin.

1404
00:51:43,635 --> 00:51:44,402
Michelob.
- Where?

1405
00:51:44,435 --> 00:51:46,103
- With his big mouth.

1406
00:51:47,305 --> 00:51:48,273
- [Joel] What?

1407
00:51:48,307 --> 00:51:49,607
It's paid for.

1408
00:51:49,640 --> 00:51:50,775
- Don't worry about
them digging in here.

1409
00:51:50,808 --> 00:51:53,145
The floors are tile.

1410
00:51:53,178 --> 00:51:54,412
- [Thorne] The walls
aren't, Doctor.

1411
00:51:54,445 --> 00:51:55,413
They're adobe.

1412
00:51:55,447 --> 00:51:56,648
- [Joel] Kill us!

1413
00:51:56,648 --> 00:51:58,617
- Our safest bet
would be on that boat.

1414
00:51:58,650 --> 00:52:00,285
- You may be right.

1415
00:52:00,318 --> 00:52:01,887
- [Tom Servo] I may be crazy.

1416
00:52:01,920 --> 00:52:04,055
- [Dr. Craigis] You can
reach your boat in daylight.

1417
00:52:04,088 --> 00:52:05,423
The shrews will
gorge themselves.

1418
00:52:05,457 --> 00:52:07,192
- [Crow] Booze is for healing.

1419
00:52:07,225 --> 00:52:10,128
- That should keep them
lethargic for several hours.

1420
00:52:10,162 --> 00:52:11,730
- There's no sense
looking at the dark side.

1421
00:52:11,763 --> 00:52:15,733
- And there's no sense
minimizing a serious situation.

1422
00:52:15,767 --> 00:52:18,270
It leaves you completely
unprepared to cope with it.

1423
00:52:18,303 --> 00:52:19,603
- [Crow] Hey!

1424
00:52:19,637 --> 00:52:20,872
- [Joel] Well you
took mine earlier.

1425
00:52:20,905 --> 00:52:22,073
- Now we certainly
can't make it tonight.

1426
00:52:22,107 --> 00:52:24,142
That's out of the question.
- Maybe tomorrow.

1427
00:52:24,175 --> 00:52:25,543
Someday, and soon!

1428
00:52:25,577 --> 00:52:27,912
- [Joel] Synchronized drinking!

1429
00:52:27,945 --> 00:52:28,813
- I have it.

1430
00:52:28,847 --> 00:52:30,182
We'll get some sleep tonight.

1431
00:52:30,248 --> 00:52:32,117
But we'll have a watch,
an hour and a half apiece.

1432
00:52:32,150 --> 00:52:34,085
Doctor, you go
first, then Radford.

1433
00:52:34,118 --> 00:52:35,120
- [Joel] I got mentioned.

1434
00:52:35,153 --> 00:52:36,120
- Jerry, and then me.

1435
00:52:36,153 --> 00:52:39,057
- [Joel] They're setting
up a Quarters game.

1436
00:52:39,090 --> 00:52:40,092
- Make sure they're
locked good and tight.

1437
00:52:40,125 --> 00:52:41,893
Check all these walls.

1438
00:52:41,927 --> 00:52:44,262
- [Crow] And roll
the brewmeister in
here so it's closer.

1439
00:52:44,295 --> 00:52:45,530
- Come now.

1440
00:52:45,563 --> 00:52:47,165
- No, I think I'll
stay here by the fire.

1441
00:52:47,198 --> 00:52:49,500
I'd feel safer.
- And closer to the bar.

1442
00:52:49,533 --> 00:52:51,002
- I couldn't stand it
in that room alone.

1443
00:52:51,035 --> 00:52:53,238
- All right, as you wish.

1444
00:52:53,272 --> 00:52:55,073
But try to get some sleep.

1445
00:52:55,107 --> 00:52:58,042
- [Tom Servo] But fart
and get some sleep?

1446
00:52:58,075 --> 00:53:01,680
- You know what I've been
thinking about, Mario?

1447
00:53:01,713 --> 00:53:03,315
- [Tom Servo] Socks,
I don't know why.

1448
00:53:03,348 --> 00:53:06,183
- Ann and that Captain.

1449
00:53:06,217 --> 00:53:07,985
- [Joel] Oh, the space
captain fantasy again.

1450
00:53:08,018 --> 00:53:09,153
- You and me.

1451
00:53:09,187 --> 00:53:11,055
- [Crow] We will need
a bigger room, then.

1452
00:53:11,088 --> 00:53:14,258
- Imagine an intelligent
girl like her

1453
00:53:14,292 --> 00:53:17,528
going for a common
sea tramp like him.

1454
00:53:20,432 --> 00:53:22,567
- [Tom Servo] Imagine in
how much detail, senor?

1455
00:53:22,600 --> 00:53:24,202
- I know why!

1456
00:53:24,235 --> 00:53:25,603
You do too.

1457
00:53:25,637 --> 00:53:26,738
- [Crow] Por que?

1458
00:53:26,772 --> 00:53:28,373
- In case anything goes wrong,

1459
00:53:28,407 --> 00:53:30,508
she's looking out
for her own hide.

1460
00:53:30,542 --> 00:53:32,010
- [Crow] 'Kay, it's typical.

1461
00:53:32,043 --> 00:53:34,378
- That's why I keep
thinking about you and me.

1462
00:53:34,412 --> 00:53:35,913
- [Joel] And Bobby McGee?

1463
00:53:35,947 --> 00:53:37,815
- Anything goes wrong?

1464
00:53:37,882 --> 00:53:40,118
- [Tom Servo] I'm not
Lisa, my name is Mario.

1465
00:53:40,152 --> 00:53:43,220
- We're gonna outlast 'em all.

1466
00:53:43,255 --> 00:53:45,523
(wind whooshing)
(thunder crashing)

1467
00:53:45,557 --> 00:53:48,225
- [Joel] Sinners repent!

1468
00:53:48,260 --> 00:53:51,597
- [Crow] Let's get
out of here, Scooby!

1469
00:53:52,663 --> 00:53:54,165
- [Joel] Shudder.

1470
00:53:57,168 --> 00:53:59,170
- I'm going to trust you.

1471
00:53:59,203 --> 00:54:01,038
- [Tom Servo] To tell
me when I've had enough.

1472
00:54:01,072 --> 00:54:03,842
- To take my turn in
patrolling the house.

1473
00:54:03,875 --> 00:54:05,377
(Joel hiccuping)

1474
00:54:05,410 --> 00:54:09,513
But when you're finished,
don't wake the Captain.

1475
00:54:10,782 --> 00:54:12,317
Come back here and get me.

1476
00:54:12,350 --> 00:54:13,852
- [Joel] Drunk.

1477
00:54:13,885 --> 00:54:17,022
- I'll probably feel good
enough by then to take his turn.

1478
00:54:17,055 --> 00:54:19,357
- [Tom Servo] He's having
his blood replaced.

1479
00:54:19,390 --> 00:54:20,525
- Okay, Mario?

1480
00:54:20,558 --> 00:54:21,693
- Si.

1481
00:54:21,727 --> 00:54:22,993
- Okay.

1482
00:54:23,027 --> 00:54:24,362
- [Joel] Don't touch me.

1483
00:54:24,395 --> 00:54:26,965
(wind whooshing)
(suspenseful music)

1484
00:54:26,998 --> 00:54:29,733
- [Tom Servo] Hmm,
let's see, I want bacon!

1485
00:54:29,767 --> 00:54:31,770
I want some bacon, yeah!

1486
00:54:34,938 --> 00:54:35,807
No bacon.

1487
00:54:35,840 --> 00:54:37,442
- No, he chewed up the slippers!

1488
00:54:37,475 --> 00:54:39,143
Bad shrew, bad shrew!

1489
00:54:42,180 --> 00:54:44,348
Little puppy?
(suspenseful music)

1490
00:54:44,382 --> 00:54:45,483
Little puppy?

1491
00:54:47,052 --> 00:54:47,818
Puppy?

1492
00:54:47,852 --> 00:54:50,855
(suspenseful music)

1493
00:54:52,523 --> 00:54:56,728
- Little puppy.
(suspenseful music)

1494
00:54:58,228 --> 00:54:59,663
- [Crow] Ahh, those shrews know

1495
00:54:59,697 --> 00:55:01,767
they're supposed
to close the door!

1496
00:55:01,800 --> 00:55:02,833
- [Joel] Now, let's see.

1497
00:55:02,867 --> 00:55:04,035
I'd better finish up those pies

1498
00:55:04,068 --> 00:55:05,137
before the shrews get them.

1499
00:55:05,170 --> 00:55:09,073
Sure is taste-tempting,
all those yummy pies.

1500
00:55:10,075 --> 00:55:13,077
(suspenseful music)

1501
00:55:16,013 --> 00:55:17,248
- [Tom Servo] Okay, right
over left, then left,

1502
00:55:17,282 --> 00:55:19,950
no, no, you've
got a granny knot!

1503
00:55:22,120 --> 00:55:24,322
(knocking)

1504
00:55:24,355 --> 00:55:25,657
- [Mario] Senor, it is Mario.

1505
00:55:25,690 --> 00:55:27,592
- [Crow] Oh, sir, pull
up the covers, please.

1506
00:55:27,625 --> 00:55:31,528
(Mario speaking
foreign language)

1507
00:55:31,562 --> 00:55:32,763
- A shrew in the cellar?

1508
00:55:32,797 --> 00:55:34,932
- Si, I hear him
singing down there.

1509
00:55:34,965 --> 00:55:35,933
- [Joel] He was singing?

1510
00:55:35,967 --> 00:55:37,135
- How did he get in?

1511
00:55:37,168 --> 00:55:39,070
- (speaking foreign
language) the kitchen window,

1512
00:55:39,103 --> 00:55:40,105
but I closed it off.

1513
00:55:40,138 --> 00:55:41,005
He went down there.

1514
00:55:41,038 --> 00:55:42,407
- Why should he go down there?

1515
00:55:42,440 --> 00:55:44,642
- The food for the little
(speaking foreign language).

1516
00:55:44,675 --> 00:55:46,643
(speaking foreign language)

1517
00:55:46,677 --> 00:55:47,912
- [Joel] What was
that about cojones?

1518
00:55:47,945 --> 00:55:48,647
- Did you tell Jerry?

1519
00:55:48,680 --> 00:55:49,447
- No, senor.

1520
00:55:49,480 --> 00:55:50,748
It is your turn next.

1521
00:55:50,815 --> 00:55:52,050
Here is (speaking
foreign language.

1522
00:55:52,083 --> 00:55:53,083
We kill him, no?

1523
00:55:53,117 --> 00:55:54,985
- [Crow] Oh, flashlight!

1524
00:55:55,018 --> 00:55:57,588
That's what he's trying to say!

1525
00:55:59,623 --> 00:56:02,627
- [Joel] It's Dave
Lennox and Dave Lennox

1526
00:56:02,660 --> 00:56:03,928
in The Lint Trap!

1527
00:56:08,633 --> 00:56:11,168
- [Tom Servo] Honey,
we're at Grandpa's, dear.

1528
00:56:11,202 --> 00:56:12,403
Wake up.

1529
00:56:12,437 --> 00:56:14,005
- [Joel] Man, I don't
mean to be rude,

1530
00:56:14,038 --> 00:56:15,407
but your eyes look like
two pee holes in the snow.

1531
00:56:15,440 --> 00:56:16,440
- [Crow] Soccer team!

1532
00:56:16,473 --> 00:56:17,942
- It's down in the cellar.

1533
00:56:17,975 --> 00:56:19,643
And we're going down after him.

1534
00:56:19,677 --> 00:56:21,747
But I don't want you to
let anybody open that door

1535
00:56:21,780 --> 00:56:22,747
'til I tell you to.

1536
00:56:22,780 --> 00:56:23,948
Understand?

1537
00:56:24,015 --> 00:56:24,915
- [Joel] Okay, anybody
can open the door

1538
00:56:24,948 --> 00:56:26,317
when you tell me.

1539
00:56:26,350 --> 00:56:28,385
Wait, wait, I
wasn't awake enough!

1540
00:56:28,420 --> 00:56:32,123
What did you say?
(suspenseful music)

1541
00:56:32,157 --> 00:56:33,257
Shrew, puppy?

1542
00:56:34,092 --> 00:56:35,760
I mean shrew!

1543
00:56:35,793 --> 00:56:37,262
- [Crow] Aw, this
is just like Aliens,

1544
00:56:37,295 --> 00:56:39,263
except without the underwear.

1545
00:56:39,297 --> 00:56:41,565
- [Tom Servo] Oh, I
like the underwear.

1546
00:56:41,598 --> 00:56:44,968
(suspenseful music)

1547
00:56:45,002 --> 00:56:46,203
- Okay, open it just a crack.

1548
00:56:46,237 --> 00:56:48,072
- [Crow] Okay.

1549
00:56:48,105 --> 00:56:49,407
- Open it.

1550
00:56:49,440 --> 00:56:50,242
- [Joel] How come
I have to open it?

1551
00:56:50,275 --> 00:56:51,308
- Hold on to it.

1552
00:56:51,342 --> 00:56:53,878
(speaking foreign language)

1553
00:56:53,912 --> 00:56:54,645
- Okay.

1554
00:56:55,580 --> 00:56:57,282
- [Tom Servo] Freeze!

1555
00:57:00,718 --> 00:57:04,055
(speaking foreign language)

1556
00:57:04,088 --> 00:57:05,123
- [Joel] Well, this is
just like that Happy Days

1557
00:57:05,157 --> 00:57:07,425
or Perfect Strangers or
Full House or Empty Nest

1558
00:57:07,458 --> 00:57:08,927
or Just the Ten of Us episode

1559
00:57:08,960 --> 00:57:11,262
when they get stuck
in the basement.

1560
00:57:11,295 --> 00:57:12,697
- [Crow] Gin, vermouth?

1561
00:57:12,730 --> 00:57:14,698
This is where they keep it all!

1562
00:57:14,732 --> 00:57:17,268
- [Tom Servo] Ooh,
we can burn all this.

1563
00:57:17,302 --> 00:57:18,703
Oh, no, there's a
Teddy Roosevelt costume

1564
00:57:18,737 --> 00:57:21,472
and some graves down here!
(Crow gasping)

1565
00:57:21,505 --> 00:57:22,873
(suspenseful music)

1566
00:57:22,907 --> 00:57:24,075
- [Joel] Ahh, there's a
Muppet behind the stairs!

1567
00:57:24,108 --> 00:57:26,310
(suspenseful music)

1568
00:57:26,343 --> 00:57:27,812
- [Crow] It's all
right under the stairs.

1569
00:57:27,845 --> 00:57:30,113
- [Tom Servo] It's all right!

1570
00:57:31,615 --> 00:57:33,985
- [Joel] Honey, I think
we got puppets down here.

1571
00:57:34,018 --> 00:57:35,253
- [Crow] Hand puppets?

1572
00:57:35,287 --> 00:57:37,855
- [Joel] They're
under the stairs,

1573
00:57:37,888 --> 00:57:41,225
so I don't think
they're marionettes.

1574
00:57:41,258 --> 00:57:43,393
- [Tom Servo] Mr. Milkbones.

1575
00:57:43,427 --> 00:57:45,062
Rawhide chew toys.

1576
00:57:47,532 --> 00:57:48,833
- Mario?

1577
00:57:48,867 --> 00:57:50,033
- [Joel] Fine, thanks.

1578
00:57:50,067 --> 00:57:50,868
- Aqui.

1579
00:57:50,902 --> 00:57:52,637
I see where he was.

1580
00:57:54,138 --> 00:57:56,040
I do not see where he is.

1581
00:57:56,073 --> 00:57:57,175
- Cuidado.

1582
00:57:57,208 --> 00:57:58,108
- Si, senor.

1583
00:57:58,142 --> 00:57:59,877
I will be careful.

1584
00:57:59,910 --> 00:58:01,245
- [Joel] Car full?

1585
00:58:01,278 --> 00:58:04,348
- [Tom Servo] Oh, no, I
got shrew doo on my shoe!

1586
00:58:04,348 --> 00:58:05,250
(suspenseful music)

1587
00:58:05,283 --> 00:58:06,050
(growling)

1588
00:58:06,083 --> 00:58:07,052
- [Joel] Ooh!

1589
00:58:07,085 --> 00:58:08,352
- [Crow] Weasels
ripped my flesh!

1590
00:58:08,385 --> 00:58:11,388
- [Tom Servo] Bad
puppet, bad puppet!

1591
00:58:12,690 --> 00:58:14,158
- [Joel] Would've
got here sooner,

1592
00:58:14,192 --> 00:58:16,193
but it's a big basement.

1593
00:58:18,362 --> 00:58:20,765
- [Crow] Please don't ask
me to suck out the venom.

1594
00:58:20,798 --> 00:58:23,200
- [Tom Servo] I thought you
said your dog does Macbeth.

1595
00:58:23,233 --> 00:58:25,603
- [Crow] He's not my dog.

1596
00:58:25,637 --> 00:58:29,507
Well, it's the booze
brothers to the rescue.

1597
00:58:29,540 --> 00:58:31,742
- [Joel] Beware the dwarf!

1598
00:58:33,410 --> 00:58:36,813
(suspenseful music)

1599
00:58:36,847 --> 00:58:38,348
- [Tom Servo] What is it, boy?

1600
00:58:38,382 --> 00:58:39,283
(gunshot)

1601
00:58:39,317 --> 00:58:40,785
- [Crow] We will prevail!

1602
00:58:40,818 --> 00:58:43,220
Our state fair is
a great state fair!

1603
00:58:43,253 --> 00:58:44,355
Try the veal.

1604
00:58:45,823 --> 00:58:47,492
- You alright down there?

1605
00:58:47,525 --> 00:58:49,327
- Doctor, get down here quick!

1606
00:58:49,360 --> 00:58:51,062
- [Crow] I'm fine, but
Mario's not doing so hot.

1607
00:58:51,095 --> 00:58:52,830
- [Joel] Oh, bad idea.

1608
00:58:52,863 --> 00:58:55,867
(suspenseful music)

1609
00:58:57,335 --> 00:58:58,670
- [Tom Servo] Hey, get off him!

1610
00:58:58,703 --> 00:59:01,338
- [Crow] No, he's got an
injury, see? (chuckling)

1611
00:59:01,372 --> 00:59:02,773
- Mario!
- Mario!

1612
00:59:04,008 --> 00:59:07,612
- [Tom Servo] Where'd
you hide the Cuervo?

1613
00:59:08,780 --> 00:59:10,515
- [Joel] Oh, he's got
rat scratch fever.

1614
00:59:10,548 --> 00:59:11,917
- [Tom Servo] Ooh!

1615
00:59:13,050 --> 00:59:14,852
(dramatic music)

1616
00:59:14,885 --> 00:59:15,953
Oh, well, look at the time.

1617
00:59:15,987 --> 00:59:19,990
I've gotta get to this
thing, I've gotta go.

1618
00:59:20,057 --> 00:59:21,058
- He's dead.

1619
00:59:22,693 --> 00:59:23,695
- [Tom Servo] He's red?

1620
00:59:23,728 --> 00:59:24,662
- [Crow] He's fed?

1621
00:59:24,695 --> 00:59:26,430
- [Joel] He's bed?

1622
00:59:26,463 --> 00:59:27,932
Oh, thank goodness!

1623
00:59:29,967 --> 00:59:31,102
- [Thorne] I got this
on him right away!

1624
00:59:31,135 --> 00:59:32,503
He couldn't have bled to death.

1625
00:59:32,537 --> 00:59:34,038
- [Tom Servo] Face
it, it's your fault.

1626
00:59:34,038 --> 00:59:35,907
- [Joel] Yep.

1627
00:59:35,940 --> 00:59:38,475
- Might as well let go of it.

1628
00:59:38,508 --> 00:59:39,843
Won't do him any good now.

1629
00:59:39,877 --> 00:59:41,778
- [Crow] Aw, get a body
bag out of the closet.

1630
00:59:41,812 --> 00:59:42,747
Can I have my gun back?

1631
00:59:42,780 --> 00:59:44,348
- What could've killed him?

1632
00:59:44,348 --> 00:59:45,817
- [Tom Servo] Oh, I don't
know, maybe that shrew?

1633
00:59:45,850 --> 00:59:48,853
- I'm not certain,
'til the autopsy.

1634
00:59:50,922 --> 00:59:52,723
- Hematoxic syndrome.

1635
00:59:52,757 --> 00:59:53,792
- [Tom Servo] Sounds
like a Ludlum book.

1636
00:59:53,825 --> 00:59:55,258
- I'm afraid so.

1637
00:59:55,293 --> 00:59:57,495
We'll know after pathology.

1638
00:59:57,528 --> 00:59:58,495
- [Crow] Scatology?

1639
00:59:58,528 --> 00:59:59,497
They study dung?

1640
00:59:59,530 --> 01:00:00,832
Ugh.

1641
01:00:00,865 --> 01:00:01,967
- That's not the same
animal you showed me.

1642
01:00:02,000 --> 01:00:03,802
That's a monster!

1643
01:00:03,835 --> 01:00:04,802
- [Joel] He grew up!

1644
01:00:04,835 --> 01:00:06,337
- They are mutants.

1645
01:00:07,538 --> 01:00:09,007
- [Crow] Ted mute-gents.

1646
01:00:09,040 --> 01:00:09,940
- In controlling
the size factor.

1647
01:00:09,973 --> 01:00:10,908
- [Joel] Ooh, that's a stretch.

1648
01:00:10,942 --> 01:00:12,177
- They seem to have crossed

1649
01:00:12,210 --> 01:00:13,778
some of the other
characteristics.

1650
01:00:13,812 --> 01:00:15,913
- Well, you certainly
did a good job of it.

1651
01:00:15,947 --> 01:00:16,947
- [Joel] Well, thank you.

1652
01:00:16,947 --> 01:00:19,117
- I've known that for
some time, Captain!

1653
01:00:19,150 --> 01:00:20,585
- [Crow] Ooh, I'm sorry.

1654
01:00:20,618 --> 01:00:22,620
I had that coming.

1655
01:00:22,653 --> 01:00:24,388
- [Joel] Now I'd like to say
a prayer, if nobody minds.

1656
01:00:24,422 --> 01:00:25,690
There, done.

1657
01:00:25,723 --> 01:00:26,723
- Mort!
- Would you please give me

1658
01:00:26,757 --> 01:00:27,725
a hand with Mario?

1659
01:00:27,758 --> 01:00:29,927
Radford, bring up the animal.

1660
01:00:29,960 --> 01:00:32,897
(dramatic music)

1661
01:00:34,098 --> 01:00:37,068
- [Joel] Tonight,
all dogs go to hell.

1662
01:00:37,102 --> 01:00:40,103
- [Tom Servo] Look,
he's levitating!

1663
01:00:41,572 --> 01:00:44,908
- [Crow] Next week
on Killer Shrews!

1664
01:00:44,942 --> 01:00:46,477
- [Tom Servo] Oh, turns
out it needs more vermouth.

1665
01:00:46,510 --> 01:00:48,578
Taste it, see what you think.

1666
01:00:48,612 --> 01:00:51,415
- Extremely high poison
content in the shrew's saliva.

1667
01:00:51,448 --> 01:00:52,717
- [Crow] But it's
smooth over ice.

1668
01:00:52,750 --> 01:00:54,852
- Now compare it with this.

1669
01:00:54,885 --> 01:00:58,088
Careful count isn't necessary.

1670
01:00:58,122 --> 01:01:00,758
Any indication the same
poison in Mario's blood

1671
01:01:00,792 --> 01:01:01,792
will give you the answer.

1672
01:01:01,825 --> 01:01:03,660
- Yes, you're right.

1673
01:01:04,962 --> 01:01:06,897
- [Tom Servo] Oh, I get it,
Mario's gonna become a shrew!

1674
01:01:06,930 --> 01:01:08,198
- Look, Ann.

1675
01:01:08,232 --> 01:01:09,100
- [Joel] You know,
you're really a drag

1676
01:01:09,133 --> 01:01:11,302
on these weekend getaways, dig?

1677
01:01:11,335 --> 01:01:13,370
- Brooding about it's
not gonna do any good.

1678
01:01:13,403 --> 01:01:14,738
- [Crow] But breeding will.

1679
01:01:14,772 --> 01:01:17,108
- Now why don't you try to
think of something else?

1680
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:18,375
Tell me.

1681
01:01:18,408 --> 01:01:19,710
- [Joel] Do you collect
plates or anything?

1682
01:01:19,743 --> 01:01:21,112
- Are you a scientist?

1683
01:01:21,145 --> 01:01:22,613
- [Joel] No, I sweep
up, what do you think?

1684
01:01:22,647 --> 01:01:23,413
- Oh?

1685
01:01:24,682 --> 01:01:26,517
That's the study of
animal act, isn't it?

1686
01:01:26,550 --> 01:01:27,585
- [Tom Servo] Animal acts?

1687
01:01:27,618 --> 01:01:28,652
- What do you specialize?

1688
01:01:28,685 --> 01:01:29,653
What do you specialize in?

1689
01:01:29,687 --> 01:01:30,655
- [Crow] Oh, nothing special.

1690
01:01:30,688 --> 01:01:31,855
- Their diet.

1691
01:01:31,888 --> 01:01:34,492
I had a hand in this, too.

1692
01:01:34,525 --> 01:01:35,727
- [Joel] If I had a hammer?

1693
01:01:35,760 --> 01:01:39,730
(wind whooshing)
(creaking)

1694
01:01:40,965 --> 01:01:42,667
- [Crow] I like
you, you're nice.

1695
01:01:42,700 --> 01:01:45,670
You're pretty, but you're
just a summer thing.

1696
01:01:45,703 --> 01:01:47,338
- But this ends it.

1697
01:01:47,372 --> 01:01:49,607
If we ever get off this island,

1698
01:01:49,640 --> 01:01:52,610
I'll never have anything
to do with it again.

1699
01:01:52,643 --> 01:01:53,710
- What will you do?

1700
01:01:53,745 --> 01:01:54,945
- [Joel] I'm going to
eat a lot of bacon.

1701
01:01:54,978 --> 01:01:57,815
- Like normal women do.

1702
01:01:57,882 --> 01:01:59,183
- [Tom Servo] Storm
the beach at Normandy?

1703
01:01:59,217 --> 01:02:02,553
- Dull after the life
I've been living.

1704
01:02:03,720 --> 01:02:06,190
I'd rather dull and
alive than excited and--

1705
01:02:06,223 --> 01:02:08,525
- I'll take a dull,
alive woman every time.

1706
01:02:08,558 --> 01:02:09,827
- [Tom Servo] I
guess the other way

1707
01:02:09,860 --> 01:02:10,662
would be kind of
sick, wouldn't it?

1708
01:02:10,695 --> 01:02:13,130
(upbeat music)

1709
01:02:17,302 --> 01:02:20,838
- [Joel] Goll, is this
hallway ever long!

1710
01:02:21,938 --> 01:02:23,842
- [Crow] Just
strain and stir it.

1711
01:02:23,875 --> 01:02:24,875
- Say Thorne.

1712
01:02:24,908 --> 01:02:26,210
- [All] Thorne.

1713
01:02:27,345 --> 01:02:30,482
- The autopsy has proved
what we suspected.

1714
01:02:30,548 --> 01:02:31,515
- [Crow] He's dead.

