01:11:28,985 --> 01:11:29,853
- Mr. Pibb.

1960
01:11:31,488 --> 01:11:34,558
- Marshmallow Peeps, lots
of Marshmallow Peeps.

1961
01:11:34,592 --> 01:11:35,858
- Okay, Marshmallow Peeps.

1962
01:11:35,892 --> 01:11:37,795
Isn't this gonna be kinda sweet?

1963
01:11:37,828 --> 01:11:39,397
- Just make the drink, barkeep.

1964
01:11:39,430 --> 01:11:40,397
SweetTarts!

1965
01:11:40,430 --> 01:11:41,532
- Vanilla frosting!

1966
01:11:41,565 --> 01:11:44,335
- Vanilla frosting,
got that over here.

1967
01:11:44,368 --> 01:11:45,502
- Wax lips.

1968
01:11:45,535 --> 01:11:46,870
- No, no, no, no wax lips.

1969
01:11:46,903 --> 01:11:48,372
You're thinking of
the Vulcan Mind Probe.

1970
01:11:48,405 --> 01:11:50,307
- All right, 86 the wax lips.

1971
01:11:50,340 --> 01:11:51,842
Now, music, maestro, please!

1972
01:11:51,875 --> 01:11:53,843
- All right, all
right, ready, okay.

1973
01:11:53,877 --> 01:11:54,812
(blender whirring)

1974
01:11:54,845 --> 01:11:55,845
- So, you live around here much?

1975
01:11:55,878 --> 01:11:57,047
- Have you seen that weather?

1976
01:11:57,113 --> 01:11:58,048
- Great hotel here, huh?

1977
01:11:58,115 --> 01:11:59,048
Been down to the pool?

1978
01:11:59,082 --> 01:12:00,383
- Aren't people here phony?

1979
01:12:00,417 --> 01:12:02,485
- All right, pour that into
the plastic tulip glass

1980
01:12:02,518 --> 01:12:05,588
and garnish with
a wind-up shrew.

1981
01:12:05,622 --> 01:12:07,323
- Hmm, you know what?

1982
01:12:07,357 --> 01:12:08,825
This looks pretty good.

1983
01:12:08,858 --> 01:12:09,960
You mind if I try it?

1984
01:12:09,993 --> 01:12:11,195
- Be my guest.

1985
01:12:13,730 --> 01:12:15,132
(thump)

1986
01:12:15,165 --> 01:12:16,433
(slurping)

1987
01:12:16,467 --> 01:12:17,500
- Whooo!

1988
01:12:18,368 --> 01:12:19,970
♪ Oh it is ladies' night

1989
01:12:20,003 --> 01:12:21,438
♪ Yeah the feeling's right

1990
01:12:21,472 --> 01:12:22,840
♪ Oh ladies' night

1991
01:12:22,873 --> 01:12:26,310
♪ Oh I want to
dance with somebody

1992
01:12:26,343 --> 01:12:28,345
♪ Whooo

1993
01:12:29,913 --> 01:12:33,183
- New rule, Frank,
don't ever touch me.

1994
01:12:34,618 --> 01:12:37,320
(upbeat music)

1995
01:12:40,857 --> 01:12:43,527
(dramatic music)

1996
01:12:45,662 --> 01:12:47,530
- [Tom Servo] Hmm, I'm fine.

1997
01:12:47,563 --> 01:12:48,865
- [Joel] Tasty.

1998
01:12:51,968 --> 01:12:53,170
(gunshot)

1999
01:12:53,203 --> 01:12:54,972
- [Joel] Here
comes the rat pack.

2000
01:12:55,005 --> 01:12:57,373
- [Tom Servo] Frank,
Sammy, Dean, Joey!

2001
01:12:57,407 --> 01:12:58,642
- [Crow] Joey?

2002
01:13:01,043 --> 01:13:03,013
- [Joel] Catch me!

2003
01:13:03,047 --> 01:13:03,980
- The shrews were out there.

2004
01:13:04,047 --> 01:13:05,115
I couldn't get the chance!

2005
01:13:05,148 --> 01:13:08,252
(all humming suspenseful music)

2006
01:13:08,285 --> 01:13:12,288
- [Joel] Never thought I'd be
so happy to see a fight scene.

2007
01:13:12,322 --> 01:13:13,290
- [Crow] Stick it to him.

2008
01:13:13,323 --> 01:13:15,125
I've got money on you!

2009
01:13:18,528 --> 01:13:21,332
- [Joel] Hey, it's
Laugh-In, look!

2010
01:13:21,365 --> 01:13:24,100
- [Crow] Swing and
a miss, wrong way.

2011
01:13:24,133 --> 01:13:28,338
(dramatic music)
(all imitating fight sounds)

2012
01:13:35,312 --> 01:13:36,313
(dramatic music)

2013
01:13:36,347 --> 01:13:37,280
- [Crow] That's illegal.

2014
01:13:37,347 --> 01:13:38,548
- For heaven's sakes,
Doctor, stop him!

2015
01:13:38,582 --> 01:13:40,750
- [Tom Servo] Doctor stop him?

2016
01:13:40,783 --> 01:13:41,952
(dramatic music)

2017
01:13:41,985 --> 01:13:44,387
- Do it, come on!
- You know you want to!

2018
01:13:44,420 --> 01:13:47,123
(all shouting)

2019
01:13:47,157 --> 01:13:48,225
(shrews chattering)

2020
01:13:48,258 --> 01:13:50,293
- [Joel] Aw, come
on, you big dummy,

2021
01:13:50,327 --> 01:13:52,595
all this stuff I gotta...

2022
01:13:52,628 --> 01:13:55,332
- [Tom Servo] I wish
I could do that.

2023
01:13:55,365 --> 01:13:59,202
(dramatic music)
(shrews screeching)

2024
01:13:59,235 --> 01:14:00,237
- [Joel] If you're not
going to buy a ticket,

2025
01:14:00,270 --> 01:14:02,338
you can't watch the game.

2026
01:14:06,243 --> 01:14:08,378
- [Crow] Well, I'll
mix up a pitcher.

2027
01:14:08,412 --> 01:14:10,547
- [Joel] You better.

2028
01:14:10,613 --> 01:14:13,850
(dramatic music)

2029
01:14:13,883 --> 01:14:17,353
- [Crow] Oh, well, I was
comforting her while you were,

2030
01:14:17,387 --> 01:14:18,322
huh-huh, gone.

2031
01:14:21,225 --> 01:14:23,893
- All right, didn't he have
it coming, or didn't he?

2032
01:14:23,927 --> 01:14:25,595
- [Tom Servo] That's your
conscience talking to you there.

2033
01:14:25,628 --> 01:14:27,030
- What happened out there?

2034
01:14:27,063 --> 01:14:28,098
- Oh, nothing much.

2035
01:14:28,132 --> 01:14:29,232
Jerry just tried
to kill me twice

2036
01:14:29,265 --> 01:14:30,700
in the last five minutes.

2037
01:14:30,733 --> 01:14:32,202
- [Joel] You know,
same old same old.

2038
01:14:32,235 --> 01:14:33,237
- [Tom Servo] Yep.

2039
01:14:33,270 --> 01:14:36,038
- Rook came ashore last night.

2040
01:14:36,072 --> 01:14:36,840
He's dead.

2041
01:14:38,342 --> 01:14:40,243
- [Crow] Or he's naked
somewhere, I don't know.

2042
01:14:40,277 --> 01:14:43,213
It's kinda leaning that way.

2043
01:14:43,247 --> 01:14:45,115
- This is all that's left.

2044
01:14:45,148 --> 01:14:48,552
Won't do us any good,
it's got no ammo.

2045
01:14:48,585 --> 01:14:50,253
- [Joel] Hey, lookie,
I found Kim Curtis,

2046
01:14:50,287 --> 01:14:51,788
TV's lovable Festus.

2047
01:14:51,822 --> 01:14:53,090
Can I keep him?

2048
01:14:56,193 --> 01:15:00,397
- [Crow] Just for that, you
can't drink for an hour.

2049
01:15:01,398 --> 01:15:03,167
- I'm deeply sorry, Captain.

2050
01:15:03,200 --> 01:15:05,168
- [Joel] Now Phillis George
is gonna make 'em hug.

2051
01:15:05,202 --> 01:15:06,737
- I wish I had
followed your orders.

2052
01:15:06,770 --> 01:15:09,573
- But Doctor, you casually
mentioned animals.

2053
01:15:09,607 --> 01:15:12,275
You didn't explain to us what
we were facing out there!

2054
01:15:12,308 --> 01:15:13,877
- [Tom Servo] Dogs with
weird stuff on 'em.

2055
01:15:13,910 --> 01:15:17,213
- You have every right
to feel the way you do.

2056
01:15:17,280 --> 01:15:20,150
My mistake was only
mine, one of judgment.

2057
01:15:20,183 --> 01:15:22,218
- [Crow] 20 lashes
with a wet noodle.

2058
01:15:22,252 --> 01:15:23,353
- I didn't know
about the hurricane.

2059
01:15:23,387 --> 01:15:24,988
I didn't anticipate the effect

2060
01:15:25,022 --> 01:15:27,323
it would have on the shrews.

2061
01:15:27,357 --> 01:15:28,492
- [Tom Servo] The
shwoo, the great shwoo?

2062
01:15:28,525 --> 01:15:30,927
- The house will be
safe for the crisis.

2063
01:15:30,960 --> 01:15:32,562
- How could you expose
your own daughter?

2064
01:15:32,595 --> 01:15:34,197
How could you
expose Ann to that?

2065
01:15:34,230 --> 01:15:35,498
- [Crow] She's adopted.

2066
01:15:35,532 --> 01:15:36,400
- She was going to
leave last week,

2067
01:15:36,433 --> 01:15:38,302
but the boat didn't come.

2068
01:15:39,402 --> 01:15:40,637
- I need a drink.

2069
01:15:42,205 --> 01:15:45,208
- [Joel] Aw, I wish you
would just get mad at me.

2070
01:15:45,242 --> 01:15:46,943
- Anybody else care for one?

2071
01:15:46,977 --> 01:15:48,745
- I could use some coffee.

2072
01:15:48,778 --> 01:15:50,280
- [Ann] I'll make some.

2073
01:15:50,280 --> 01:15:51,080
- Thank you, my dear.

2074
01:15:51,080 --> 01:15:52,082
- [Tom Servo] Good idea.

2075
01:15:52,115 --> 01:15:53,117
- Cream and sugar?

2076
01:15:53,150 --> 01:15:54,652
(shrew screeching)
(dramatic music)

2077
01:15:54,685 --> 01:15:58,155
- Oh, my leg!
(dramatic music)

2078
01:15:58,188 --> 01:15:59,155
- [Tom Servo] Stay, stay!

2079
01:15:59,188 --> 01:16:00,190
(gunshots)
You stay!

2080
01:16:00,223 --> 01:16:01,023
Stay, sit!

2081
01:16:02,192 --> 01:16:03,160
Good dog.
(gunshot)

2082
01:16:03,193 --> 01:16:05,162
Stay, good dog.

2083
01:16:05,195 --> 01:16:07,197
- [Joel] Well, I'm dead.

2084
01:16:08,232 --> 01:16:10,200
- You all right, Doctor?

2085
01:16:10,233 --> 01:16:12,168
- I just ripped my
trousers, that's all.

2086
01:16:12,202 --> 01:16:13,237
- [Joel] I'm fine, really.

2087
01:16:13,270 --> 01:16:14,872
- [Tom Servo] Uh-oh.

2088
01:16:19,075 --> 01:16:21,345
- [Crow] The end.

2089
01:16:21,378 --> 01:16:24,347
- [Joel] Yeah, enjoy
in moderation, my ass.

2090
01:16:24,347 --> 01:16:27,383
(dramatic music)

2091
01:16:27,417 --> 01:16:29,887
(gunshots)
- Oh!

2092
01:16:29,920 --> 01:16:33,657
- [Joel] Okay, you'd
better switch to coffee.

2093
01:16:34,825 --> 01:16:37,995
- [Tom Servo] The
money is in the, uh...

2094
01:16:40,330 --> 01:16:41,332
- There's still four
of 'em in there!

2095
01:16:41,365 --> 01:16:44,868
- [Joel] My hair, I
leave to Steve Allen.

2096
01:16:46,370 --> 01:16:49,205
My sport coat I leave to Bamuha.

2097
01:16:50,507 --> 01:16:53,643
- [Crow] Wow, he really
cruised those five stages.

2098
01:16:53,677 --> 01:16:55,712
- [Ann] Radford!

2099
01:16:55,745 --> 01:16:59,950
- [Crow] Look at him, he looks
weird without his glasses.

2100
01:17:00,817 --> 01:17:03,620
(dramatic music)

2101
01:17:03,653 --> 01:17:04,855
- He's dead.

2102
01:17:04,888 --> 01:17:06,757
- Now who'll pay
his part of the tab?

2103
01:17:06,790 --> 01:17:09,625
- [Tom Servo] Check his wallet.

2104
01:17:09,660 --> 01:17:12,162
(dramatic music)

2105
01:17:12,195 --> 01:17:13,597
- [Joel] What's this say here?

2106
01:17:13,630 --> 01:17:15,498
Short little kraut?

2107
01:17:15,532 --> 01:17:17,100
Wait a minute,
conditions hellish?

2108
01:17:17,133 --> 01:17:18,535
What's going on here?

2109
01:17:18,568 --> 01:17:20,770
Mary Dawn Deardon.

2110
01:17:20,803 --> 01:17:24,007
- He recorded every
symptom and reaction,

2111
01:17:24,040 --> 01:17:25,942
right up to the
moment of his death.

2112
01:17:25,975 --> 01:17:28,278
- [Crow] But he's
a terrible speller.

2113
01:17:28,312 --> 01:17:29,412
Was with a Z.

2114
01:17:30,613 --> 01:17:31,348
- Jerry, tear down
one of those drapes

2115
01:17:31,415 --> 01:17:32,448
and cover him up.

2116
01:17:32,482 --> 01:17:34,250
- [Joel] Tear down a drink?

2117
01:17:34,283 --> 01:17:36,720
- Sure, I guess I'll cover him.

2118
01:17:39,322 --> 01:17:42,525
You'll cover me, but
who'll cover you?

2119
01:17:44,193 --> 01:17:47,830
- [Joel] Hey, is this one
of them funny joke riddles?

2120
01:17:47,863 --> 01:17:49,432
(blow landing)

2121
01:17:49,465 --> 01:17:50,233
- [Joel] She's my sister!

2122
01:17:50,267 --> 01:17:51,300
She's my daughter!

2123
01:17:51,333 --> 01:17:52,835
(blow landing)

2124
01:17:52,868 --> 01:17:53,737
- [Tom Servo] Well,
somebody's going to jail,

2125
01:17:53,770 --> 01:17:55,272
and it's not gonna be me!

2126
01:17:55,305 --> 01:17:59,042
- [Jerry] It'd take a tank
to get us out of here!

2127
01:17:59,075 --> 01:18:01,177
(suspenseful music)

2128
01:18:01,210 --> 01:18:02,245
- Look!

2129
01:18:03,447 --> 01:18:04,748
There!

2130
01:18:04,782 --> 01:18:06,583
(dramatic music)

2131
01:18:06,617 --> 01:18:07,550
- [Crow] Hello, Doreen.

2132
01:18:07,583 --> 01:18:08,785
Hello, Shirley.

2133
01:18:08,818 --> 01:18:11,722
(shrew chittering)

2134
01:18:11,755 --> 01:18:15,792
- [Joel] Not the couch, I
just had it upholstered!

2135
01:18:15,825 --> 01:18:17,227
- [Tom Servo] That's nice, good.

2136
01:18:17,260 --> 01:18:18,762
Now the lamp, the
lamp would look nice.

2137
01:18:18,795 --> 01:18:21,698
Get the floor lamp and
bring it over here.

2138
01:18:21,732 --> 01:18:23,267
- It won't take them
long to dig around this.

2139
01:18:23,300 --> 01:18:24,600
- You're right.

2140
01:18:24,633 --> 01:18:27,270
Not telling where else
they're digging, too.

2141
01:18:27,303 --> 01:18:30,840
(dramatic music)
- Uh-oh.

2142
01:18:32,742 --> 01:18:35,278
- [Crow] Quick,
get another couch!

2143
01:18:35,312 --> 01:18:37,247
- [Joel] No, not the wet bar!

2144
01:18:37,247 --> 01:18:41,217
(mock sobbing)
(dramatic music)

2145
01:18:45,022 --> 01:18:47,723
- [Tom Servo] That'll hold 'em.

2146
01:18:48,558 --> 01:18:50,093
- Come on, the patio.

2147
01:18:50,127 --> 01:18:52,362
- [Tom Servo] Tooky-tooky.

2148
01:18:56,032 --> 01:18:58,802
- [Joel] We're
gonna barbecue now?

2149
01:19:00,970 --> 01:19:03,005
(Crow munching)

2150
01:19:03,038 --> 01:19:04,775
- Out here to
barricade those walls.

2151
01:19:04,808 --> 01:19:06,375
I'll tell you, we'll pile
some of those crates up

2152
01:19:06,408 --> 01:19:08,345
over there, and that
roof's our last chance.

2153
01:19:08,378 --> 01:19:10,413
- [Tom Servo] We're
gonna put on a show!

2154
01:19:10,447 --> 01:19:11,715
- Find something light!

2155
01:19:11,715 --> 01:19:16,352
(dramatic music)
(shrews chittering)

2156
01:19:16,385 --> 01:19:19,022
- [Joel] Hey, this is my beat!

2157
01:19:20,223 --> 01:19:21,223
- Here, help her
with that, Doctor!

2158
01:19:21,257 --> 01:19:24,193
Jerry, see if you
can find some rope.

2159
01:19:27,097 --> 01:19:28,198
- [Crow] Hey!

2160
01:19:29,132 --> 01:19:31,602
I found a wheat penny!

2161
01:19:31,635 --> 01:19:32,935
I'm keeping it.

2162
01:19:34,905 --> 01:19:36,372
- [Tom Servo] I found
some great stuff in here.

2163
01:19:36,405 --> 01:19:37,673
Check it out.

2164
01:19:37,707 --> 01:19:39,208
Golf clubs, and--
- Oh, he must be

2165
01:19:39,242 --> 01:19:41,210
the Dr. Smith of this movie.

2166
01:19:41,243 --> 01:19:45,182
- Doctor, we can use these
chemical drums as tanks.

2167
01:19:45,215 --> 01:19:46,750
Individual tanks!

2168
01:19:48,017 --> 01:19:51,187
- [Crow] Sort of like
a personal pan pizza!

2169
01:19:51,220 --> 01:19:53,357
- [Thorne] Set it down now.

2170
01:19:53,390 --> 01:19:55,558
- [Joel] Oh, it's
really cool in here.

2171
01:19:55,592 --> 01:19:57,893
Bang a hammer on it for me.

2172
01:19:59,595 --> 01:20:01,463
- [Joel] That, no, nothing,
nothing, wasn't doing anything.

2173
01:20:01,498 --> 01:20:05,702
Just standing around
back here. (whistling)

2174
01:20:07,103 --> 01:20:08,405
- It'll work!

2175
01:20:08,438 --> 01:20:10,140
It'll work!

2176
01:20:10,173 --> 01:20:12,508
- I'm too tall for the base.

2177
01:20:12,542 --> 01:20:15,178
If the shrews don't push
us over, the wind will.

2178
01:20:15,212 --> 01:20:16,378
- Not if we lash them together!

2179
01:20:16,412 --> 01:20:17,613
- [Joel] Well,
they're not really

2180
01:20:17,680 --> 01:20:19,548
personal tanks
anymore, are they?

2181
01:20:19,582 --> 01:20:21,785
- Only that one over there?

2182
01:20:21,818 --> 01:20:22,785
- [Tom Servo] Where?

2183
01:20:22,818 --> 01:20:23,787
Oh.

2184
01:20:23,820 --> 01:20:26,322
(men shouting)

2185
01:20:27,523 --> 01:20:30,693
- [Tom Servo] I'm gonna
put a wet bar in mine!

2186
01:20:30,727 --> 01:20:32,128
- Hey, know what?

2187
01:20:32,162 --> 01:20:34,230
I bet we could do
something with these wigs!

2188
01:20:34,263 --> 01:20:36,767
(clattering)

2189
01:20:38,033 --> 01:20:41,605
- [Joel] Yeah, help
out a little bit.

2190
01:20:41,638 --> 01:20:43,105
Hmm, bigger than the other one!

2191
01:20:43,138 --> 01:20:44,540
- [Crow] What a coinky-dink.

2192
01:20:44,573 --> 01:20:47,277
- [Tom Servo] What,
Shrew Be Gone?

2193
01:20:47,310 --> 01:20:49,178
We're saved, ha ha!

2194
01:20:49,212 --> 01:20:50,780
(shrews chittering)

2195
01:20:50,847 --> 01:20:52,748
- [Crow] What are they doing?

2196
01:20:52,782 --> 01:20:54,850
Oh, it's Flashdance.

2197
01:20:54,885 --> 01:20:56,587
He's an exotic dancer at night.

2198
01:20:56,620 --> 01:20:58,120
- [Joel] He's a maniac.

2199
01:20:58,153 --> 01:20:59,655
- [Crow] He's a maniac.

2200
01:20:59,688 --> 01:21:02,192
(upbeat music)

2201
01:21:06,997 --> 01:21:10,033
- Get some rope and
put it on that latch

2202
01:21:10,067 --> 01:21:12,435
so we can raise it
from the ground.

2203
01:21:12,468 --> 01:21:13,937
- [Joel] It's all
the same to Mary Lou,

2204
01:21:13,970 --> 01:21:18,140
calf riding, broody contests,
escaping killer shrews.

2205
01:21:18,173 --> 01:21:18,942
